1
00:00:01,960 --> 00:02:03,760
Visit our website for more: turkision.com

2
00:02:03,950 --> 00:02:08,270
No living being was harmed
during the filming of this series.

3
00:02:08,970 --> 00:02:11,870
Episode 119

4
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:16,370
Every soul will taste death, my dear.

5
00:02:17,210 --> 00:02:22,420
As the apostles and prophets
pass into the eternal world...

6
00:02:22,890 --> 00:02:26,410
we'll leave when the time is right.

7
00:02:27,060 --> 00:02:35,080
How happy we offer our soul for the sake of truth
and write our name with the martyrs.

8
00:02:36,310 --> 00:02:44,810
What we should do is to carry the banner they left us and pass it on from generation to generation.

9
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:47,500
Inshallah.

10
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:53,870
If there is a painful side to death...

11
00:02:54,310 --> 00:02:59,640
It is the longing of the living
for those who are gone.

12
00:03:00,250 --> 00:03:04,530
But the world is strange.

13
00:03:04,820 --> 00:03:08,940
The home of alienation is a place
where we suffer from longing.

14
00:03:09,370 --> 00:03:12,520
Our meeting is at home.

15
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:20,890
May Allah make it our share to meet
in the abode of survival.

16
00:03:21,210 --> 00:03:22,570
Amin.

17
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:24,960
Amin.

18
00:03:26,510 --> 00:03:30,330
Amin, my Sheikh.

19
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:39,890
Bengi Hatun, don't be sad.

20
00:03:40,140 --> 00:03:42,420
Don't think pessimistic.

21
00:03:46,050 --> 00:03:51,970
We will avenge Öktem Bey
and everyone else.

22
00:03:54,270 --> 00:03:59,070
I bellieve, you will not leave our
blood on the ground, however...

23
00:04:00,330 --> 00:04:04,840
Will you avenge us by being under
the command of Nayman, Osman Bey?

24
00:04:11,779 --> 00:04:15,440
If you want death to stop at Öktem...

25
00:04:16,470 --> 00:04:19,240
You will obey my command, Osman.

26
00:04:19,290 --> 00:04:22,370
If you do not enter into my command...

27
00:04:22,530 --> 00:04:27,550
I will kill all your loved
ones in front of your eyes.

28
00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:39,200
I give you time until tomorrow.

29
00:04:39,980 --> 00:04:41,580
Make up your mind.

30
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:44,030
Either you come under my command...

31
00:04:44,030 --> 00:04:48,520
Or you bury your loved ones
under the soil.

32
00:04:56,490 --> 00:05:02,370
Who of my family are you going to
sacrifice this time to take your revenge?

33
00:05:03,590 --> 00:05:05,810
Don't, Osman Bey.

34
00:05:05,870 --> 00:05:09,550
Don't ever touch anyone in my family.

35
00:05:10,940 --> 00:05:15,990
If you are going to sacrifice anyone,
let it be me, Osman Bey.

36
00:05:20,450 --> 00:05:22,600
Bengi Hatun.

37
00:05:24,650 --> 00:05:27,490
Your words are sharper than a dagger.

38
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:37,600
I know, I know you're hurt.

39
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:43,760
But we will be relatives soon.

40
00:05:44,990 --> 00:05:47,360
Never forget this.

41
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:53,760
Öktem Bey offered
his head for the calling.

42
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:58,260
And tomorrow it will be Osman Bey.

43
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:02,900
Our calling is greater than everything.

44
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:07,280
I know for sure.

45
00:06:07,860 --> 00:06:12,350
You are in pain and the pain
is gnawing at your heart.

46
00:06:13,620 --> 00:06:15,400
However...

47
00:06:16,890 --> 00:06:20,920
Never forget how great our calling is.

48
00:06:23,740 --> 00:06:25,630
Can I come in, my Bey?

49
00:06:25,900 --> 00:06:27,520
Come in.

50
00:06:33,190 --> 00:06:35,130
My sheikh.

51
00:06:35,610 --> 00:06:38,480
Nayman has gone to Söğüt.

52
00:06:38,590 --> 00:06:40,830
And he met Mother Sultan.

53
00:06:54,670 --> 00:06:57,030
He must have gone to hold her accountable.

54
00:06:57,450 --> 00:07:00,520
But we cannot know on which
side Mother Sultan will stand.

55
00:07:00,810 --> 00:07:02,910
We will take our precautions...

56
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:05,400
to understand the situation.

57
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:09,290
Who will we trust, Osman Bey?

58
00:07:09,550 --> 00:07:13,380
How do we know that İsmihan Sultan
will not sell us out?

59
00:07:15,180 --> 00:07:19,970
Nayman will extend his hand to
her and ask for her friendship.

60
00:07:22,470 --> 00:07:25,080
Who will we trust, Osman Bey?

61
00:07:25,590 --> 00:07:30,440
The man who killed my husband is extending
one hand to us and the other to İsmihan.

62
00:07:30,590 --> 00:07:32,860
Who will we trust?

63
00:07:33,850 --> 00:07:37,080
It's okay to hold the hand that
reaches out to us for help.

64
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:39,020
We respect it.

65
00:07:39,060 --> 00:07:42,490
But if that hand is
extended to break us..

66
00:07:44,050 --> 00:07:46,960
We will not leave bones in it, Inshallah.

67
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:51,160
They both reached out to break.

68
00:07:52,420 --> 00:07:54,390
We will not forget this.

69
00:07:56,930 --> 00:07:59,430
We will not leave him unpunished.

70
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:02,640
Nayman fights with his army.

71
00:08:03,260 --> 00:08:05,030
İsmihan fights with her tricks.

72
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:06,820
If united...

73
00:08:06,930 --> 00:08:08,610
It will be difficult for us.

74
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:11,290
Let's stop Nayman first.

75
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:15,750
And then it will be the
turn of Mother Sultan.

76
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:20,350
But it's still too early for that.

77
00:08:22,810 --> 00:08:24,710
Söğüt

78
00:08:27,610 --> 00:08:33,350
You pretended to be loyal
to me and united with Osman.

79
00:08:34,058 --> 00:08:35,960
I did what's necessary.

80
00:08:36,090 --> 00:08:40,480
Is it necessary to betray me, woman?

81
00:08:42,140 --> 00:08:45,200
Do you not want to be
accepted into this land?

82
00:08:45,770 --> 00:08:48,360
Olof killed many people here.

83
00:08:48,550 --> 00:08:53,680
His life would have hurt you, Nayman.

84
00:08:54,660 --> 00:08:59,460
If someone dies, I decide that.

85
00:08:59,710 --> 00:09:03,050
And if anyone survives, I decide that.

86
00:09:03,180 --> 00:09:06,760
Neither you nor Osman.

87
00:09:09,260 --> 00:09:17,750
Until Osman is by my side,
you will never be with him again.

88
00:09:27,450 --> 00:09:31,890
Do you think Osman will
come under your command?

89
00:09:36,080 --> 00:09:38,570
I don't think, İsmihan

90
00:09:38,940 --> 00:09:40,520
I know this.

91
00:09:43,340 --> 00:09:46,360
What is your goal, Nayman?

92
00:09:46,860 --> 00:09:49,070
My goal...

93
00:09:49,570 --> 00:09:57,540
is so big that neither
you nor Osman can understand it.

94
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:04,240
Whatever your goal is...

95
00:10:04,750 --> 00:10:06,860
I know Osman bey very well.

96
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:09,550
He isn't good at trading

97
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:14,510
He offers his head, but does not
come under your command.

98
00:10:15,020 --> 00:10:16,920
This is a mistake.

99
00:10:18,520 --> 00:10:21,650
Osman will come
under my command.

100
00:10:21,950 --> 00:10:25,790
And it will happen thanks to you.

101
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:33,830
If I can help you, that's
great, Commander Nayman.

102
00:10:34,910 --> 00:10:36,170
But I don't think so.

103
00:10:40,350 --> 00:10:44,240
I am always beside you.

104
00:10:44,720 --> 00:10:48,520
And ready to do whatever it takes, Nayman.

105
00:10:49,310 --> 00:10:52,780
What does it take for Osman?

106
00:10:53,690 --> 00:10:58,500
What you said a while ago was true.

107
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:03,680
Osman is a bad trader.

108
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:08,000
He gives his soul and does
not take orders from anyone.

109
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:11,890
Even you couldn't stop him.

110
00:11:12,140 --> 00:11:17,600
But he will come to protect his people.

111
00:11:18,570 --> 00:11:21,620
I'm always with you, Nayman.

112
00:11:22,410 --> 00:11:25,160
I'm ready to do what it takes.

113
00:11:26,750 --> 00:11:31,540
I don't think you
understand, Mother Sultan.

114
00:11:33,460 --> 00:11:35,470
Soldier.

115
00:11:36,940 --> 00:11:39,720
Send a messenger to Konya.

116
00:11:39,940 --> 00:11:43,600
Tell them, if Mother Sultan disobeys me...

117
00:11:43,890 --> 00:11:50,120
the head of her son Aladdin will be hung
at the entrance to Konya.

118
00:11:57,130 --> 00:12:00,730
And now you understand, Mother Sultan.

119
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:06,500
All of you are at my command.

120
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:13,000
And all your souls rest upon my sword.

121
00:12:32,070 --> 00:12:36,700
Mother Sultan will
calm Nayman and calm the atmosphere.

122
00:12:36,850 --> 00:12:39,200
And he will think that his
campaign has succeeded.

123
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:45,290
And then I will put my sword on
the neck of Mother Sultan.

124
00:12:50,330 --> 00:12:53,980
Why would Nayman stop?

125
00:12:54,620 --> 00:12:57,760
Why would they tolerate us when
the opportunity was in his hand?

126
00:12:58,400 --> 00:13:01,470
Do you see that he has taken it easy on us
after all, Turgut Bey?

127
00:13:01,620 --> 00:13:05,660
- Don't you consider losing my husband a loss?
- Bengi Hatun, stop.

128
00:13:06,410 --> 00:13:09,430
Your pain is our pain, and
our pain is great.

129
00:13:10,670 --> 00:13:13,610
My question is different from that.

130
00:13:14,430 --> 00:13:23,140
I'm talking about Nayman, who can attack our lands, what will make him stop now?

131
00:13:24,680 --> 00:13:26,840
We understood that he
would not attack us...

132
00:13:26,850 --> 00:13:30,350
but what does it mean that he wants you
under his command, Osman Bey?

133
00:13:32,010 --> 00:13:34,360
I don't know why he did this.

134
00:13:37,070 --> 00:13:41,340
I thought he did it
to win his army a crushing victory.

135
00:13:41,670 --> 00:13:47,460
But he silenced all the Beys
and separated us.

136
00:13:49,380 --> 00:13:51,100
He must have another goal.

137
00:13:53,100 --> 00:13:55,210
He must have a greater purpose than that.

138
00:13:57,530 --> 00:13:59,690
How will we know this goal?

139
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:02,000
Did you keep the prisoners?

140
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:06,050
We captured the three Mongol soldiers that
Nayman gave to Olof and set the rest free.

141
00:14:06,110 --> 00:14:09,350
We'll interrogate
the prisoners first to find out.

142
00:14:09,580 --> 00:14:12,320
Meanwhile, distribute the
Beys' share of the gold.

143
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:16,100
- Let's do what we have to do.
- Your command, my Bey.

144
00:14:18,050 --> 00:14:22,050
You bear this burden, but there are
other heavy burdens, Osman Bey.

145
00:14:22,690 --> 00:14:27,200
We ask Allah not to burden us with
what we can't carry. Do not worry at all.

146
00:14:28,190 --> 00:14:30,280
We will definitely get through that.

147
00:14:33,770 --> 00:14:36,250
If you excue me, my Sheikh.

148
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:48,990
Let each of you go to your job.

149
00:14:55,910 --> 00:14:58,170
My Bey, what is your purpose
from these prisoners?

150
00:14:58,220 --> 00:15:00,840
We'll wreak havoc with
them in the Nyman army.

151
00:15:01,570 --> 00:15:03,500
Shall we do it with two
or three soldiers, my Bey?

152
00:15:03,710 --> 00:15:06,600
We will destroy Nayman's campaign.

153
00:15:07,010 --> 00:15:10,430
Tell me, do you know the
story of David and Goliath?

154
00:15:13,510 --> 00:15:16,270
David was weaker than Goliath.

155
00:15:16,950 --> 00:15:19,870
But he knew all his weaknesses.

156
00:15:20,150 --> 00:15:21,950
And these captives will be so for us.

157
00:15:22,430 --> 00:15:25,520
They will be the first stone
that David will throw at Goliath.

158
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:30,690
We will scatter Nayman's army completely.

159
00:15:39,890 --> 00:15:43,970
Osman Bey is coming!

160
00:16:04,740 --> 00:16:08,310
You're the remnants of swords that
do not know for whom you are fighting.

161
00:16:08,690 --> 00:16:10,550
You are right, Osman.

162
00:16:10,950 --> 00:16:14,180
It doesn't matter who I'm fighting for...

163
00:16:14,265 --> 00:16:18,285
but the important thing is that I
hold my sword against you.

164
00:16:22,090 --> 00:16:27,400
Nayman used you against Olof.

165
00:16:31,670 --> 00:16:33,910
While you had many dreams...

166
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:37,520
and the battles you would have fought...

167
00:16:37,970 --> 00:16:42,960
We still have these dreams.
Kill me that God embraces me.

168
00:16:43,130 --> 00:16:46,130
Our goal is to erase people like you.

169
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:49,930
And this will be your end, whether
we die or live.

170
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:56,920
Tell me who we are.

171
00:16:57,550 --> 00:16:59,230
You are the Muslims

172
00:16:59,910 --> 00:17:04,130
We will drain your offspring and
destroy your sanctities.

173
00:17:06,770 --> 00:17:12,520
We rebelled against our own for that
and turned our backs on Ghazan Khan.

174
00:17:12,750 --> 00:17:14,670
We will erase you, Osman.

175
00:17:15,040 --> 00:17:19,560
Your Allah, whom
you trust, will not benefit you.

176
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:28,970
It's time to tell you the bad news.

177
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:34,920
So know the truth about the man you are under.

178
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:40,780
Commander Nayman was honored by the
grace of Islam on these Muslim lands...

179
00:17:42,670 --> 00:17:47,970
that he came to sweep with his armies.

180
00:17:49,460 --> 00:17:51,560
Is it true what you say, Osman Bey?

181
00:17:53,670 --> 00:17:58,890
He says your case is over.

182
00:18:24,610 --> 00:18:27,240
We've watched the roads as
you have commanded...

183
00:18:27,250 --> 00:18:30,730
and Nayman's caravan will
come to our lands tomorrow.

184
00:18:31,370 --> 00:18:33,860
They came from the way
you told us, Osman Bey.

185
00:18:34,320 --> 00:18:37,600
This is the second stone that
we will throw in the face of Goliath.

186
00:18:38,910 --> 00:18:41,620
We'll throw it at the right time so that
it will benefit our campaign more.

187
00:18:41,740 --> 00:18:43,870
Your campaign, Osman Bey.

188
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:49,830
My Bey, they asked me to
deliver this letter to you.

189
00:18:57,310 --> 00:18:59,010
From whom is this letter?

190
00:19:02,120 --> 00:19:06,250
For those who carry their secrets with
their hearts and not with their minds.

191
00:19:10,970 --> 00:19:13,440
- I'll go to them.
- Okay.

192
00:19:21,730 --> 00:19:24,030
Öktem tribe

193
00:19:25,180 --> 00:19:27,580
Bengi Hatun is coming!

194
00:19:38,930 --> 00:19:41,340
The chair is empty, Bengi Hatun.

195
00:19:42,490 --> 00:19:47,030
We have to hold a council to choose a Bey,
as Öktem Bey has no son.

196
00:19:49,320 --> 00:19:51,820
The chair must find someone to occupy it.

197
00:19:52,340 --> 00:19:56,050
Tell me which chair was left
empty, so our chair remained empty?

198
00:20:03,960 --> 00:20:08,760
What is the urgency? Yesterday, I buried
my husband's body in the dirt.

199
00:20:09,810 --> 00:20:12,710
But I see that your voices
are rising in this regard.

200
00:20:14,020 --> 00:20:17,170
You are crying over the empty chair today.

201
00:20:17,730 --> 00:20:19,790
But if I order you tomorrow and...

202
00:20:19,830 --> 00:20:26,120
tell you that we will stand against Nayman
who killed my husband and our children...

203
00:20:26,290 --> 00:20:31,190
What will be the situation?
Will your voices rise then?

204
00:20:37,790 --> 00:20:39,230
It won't.

205
00:20:42,220 --> 00:20:46,710
Your voices only get louder in my tent.

206
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:53,420
Your Bey was martyred without
blinking an eyelid out of fear of death.

207
00:20:56,870 --> 00:21:00,670
But what about you?

208
00:21:02,120 --> 00:21:05,320
Can you be brave like him?

209
00:21:07,870 --> 00:21:11,390
Raise your voice now, come on.

210
00:21:12,240 --> 00:21:16,610
Nayman is the commander of a large army,
and you know the number of our warriors.

211
00:21:16,870 --> 00:21:18,960
What can we do against him?

212
00:21:19,620 --> 00:21:24,930
You will then let the blood of your Bey
and your children be in vain, will you not?

213
00:21:31,440 --> 00:21:36,700
You can't do anything
with your cowardice.

214
00:21:37,140 --> 00:21:41,480
- Osman Bey will punish Nayman.
- He will certainly punish him.

215
00:21:42,680 --> 00:21:45,650
But Osman often goes on and on.

216
00:21:46,170 --> 00:21:50,340
Those who have been killed is
from our tribe.

217
00:21:52,630 --> 00:21:55,780
And I will not waste time with the
politics that Osman follows.

218
00:21:57,930 --> 00:22:02,600
But I see at the same time that
this will not happen to you.

219
00:22:04,340 --> 00:22:07,040
When I say Nayman, your hearts tremble.

220
00:22:07,110 --> 00:22:11,690
That is why
none of you have the right to this chair.

221
00:22:17,480 --> 00:22:24,450
A hero who doesn't accept that Öktem Bey's
blood should be in vain must sit in this chair.

222
00:22:30,870 --> 00:22:35,730
And until he
comes, I'll sit on this chair.

223
00:22:41,550 --> 00:22:45,400
It's up to you, Bengi Hatun,
but who is this hero you speak of?

224
00:22:48,620 --> 00:22:52,660
- Can I come in?
- Come in.

225
00:22:56,700 --> 00:22:59,780
Bengi Hatun, Bala Hatun and
her attendants are here.

226
00:23:00,360 --> 00:23:01,820
Go ahead.

227
00:23:05,670 --> 00:23:08,200
Now you get out, come on.

228
00:23:38,440 --> 00:23:42,940
- Salam Alaikum.
- Alaikum Salam.

229
00:23:45,330 --> 00:23:46,440
Well, Bengi Hatun...

230
00:23:47,130 --> 00:23:49,010
Why are Beys here?

231
00:23:50,070 --> 00:23:52,100
And what will it be, Bala Hatun?

232
00:23:52,540 --> 00:23:55,500
They ask what we will do
after losing Öktem Bey.

233
00:23:56,660 --> 00:23:59,230
Is this reasonable at a time like this?

234
00:23:59,890 --> 00:24:02,010
We have recently buried Öktem Bey.

235
00:24:02,790 --> 00:24:05,780
They see it right, Ayşe Hatun.

236
00:24:06,540 --> 00:24:08,980
So that the chair
does not remain empty.

237
00:24:14,330 --> 00:24:16,760
It's good that you came, for
I was coming to you.

238
00:24:18,140 --> 00:24:20,220
- Please be seated.
- No, thank you.

239
00:24:20,700 --> 00:24:22,620
We have come to say our
condolences.

240
00:24:23,290 --> 00:24:25,430
Well, what were
you going to tell us?

241
00:24:32,180 --> 00:24:35,550
The matter of Aktemur and Alçiçek has
been around for a long time.

242
00:24:36,520 --> 00:24:39,050
I say let's tie the knot right away.

243
00:24:41,290 --> 00:24:42,290
Mother!

244
00:24:43,210 --> 00:24:47,620
Do you hear what you're saying?
My father is dead.

245
00:24:52,270 --> 00:24:56,870
Alçiçek is right, this isn't appropriate until
40 days have passed since Öktem Bey's death.

246
00:24:57,200 --> 00:24:58,750
Öktem is a martyr.

247
00:25:02,460 --> 00:25:04,460
He does not want us to mourn him.

248
00:25:10,520 --> 00:25:13,100
This issue has dragged on for a long time.

249
00:25:13,530 --> 00:25:16,680
We have to shut people's mouths.

250
00:25:19,260 --> 00:25:20,660
Bengi Hatun.

251
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:23,710
I don't think Aktemur
would agree to that.

252
00:25:24,010 --> 00:25:26,480
Listen to me and
let's wait a little longer.

253
00:25:26,790 --> 00:25:29,390
- At least...
- I said what I said.

254
00:25:33,740 --> 00:25:36,630
Either the wedding will
take place on the spot...

255
00:25:37,080 --> 00:25:39,150
or we
cancel the engagement.

256
00:25:45,880 --> 00:25:48,170
- It's up to you.
- Bengi Hatun.

257
00:25:55,840 --> 00:25:59,160
Why this hurry? There is a
funeral at your house.

258
00:26:00,150 --> 00:26:02,120
Is there something
we don't know?

259
00:26:10,320 --> 00:26:12,810
Tell me, what is Nayman's main
campaign?

260
00:26:13,240 --> 00:26:20,870
The conversion of Ghazan Mahmud Khan
has caused much confusion.

261
00:26:21,200 --> 00:26:23,860
Among his commanders and
even among the Mongol forces.

262
00:26:24,400 --> 00:26:28,470
Sülemiş rebelled because
he was not given the sovereignty of Anatolia.

263
00:26:29,060 --> 00:26:34,970
Nayman and his brother Talay
want to expand that rebellion.

264
00:26:36,300 --> 00:26:37,300
Good.

265
00:26:38,990 --> 00:26:41,090
Everyone will live
as they deserve.

266
00:26:41,960 --> 00:26:43,650
Let them mess with each other.

267
00:26:44,530 --> 00:26:46,870
But their main goal
is to create a state.

268
00:26:47,810 --> 00:26:50,540
Talay gathers the army in
the Mamluk state.

269
00:26:50,930 --> 00:26:53,070
And Nayman is
getting stronger here.

270
00:26:54,670 --> 00:26:57,760
That is why Nayman did not want
to use all his power against us.

271
00:27:00,660 --> 00:27:02,900
Their campaign is fueled
by the enemies of Islam.

272
00:27:04,500 --> 00:27:11,290
But the alliance that they are preparing for
will inflict injustice on Islamic lands only.

273
00:27:12,530 --> 00:27:13,730
Don't ever worry.

274
00:27:14,810 --> 00:27:17,960
I will prevent it as long as I breathe.

275
00:27:18,840 --> 00:27:22,320
That's why your state lives.

276
00:27:22,850 --> 00:27:26,960
You have the strength, courage
and ability, Osman Bey.

277
00:27:27,980 --> 00:27:30,140
Only you can stop them.

278
00:27:33,080 --> 00:27:34,720
Thank you.

279
00:27:48,130 --> 00:27:49,220
It is from the caliph.

280
00:28:21,600 --> 00:28:22,600
Talk.

281
00:28:23,730 --> 00:28:25,920
What is happening in Konya?

282
00:28:26,970 --> 00:28:29,180
Konya is in our hands, Commander Nayman.

283
00:28:30,070 --> 00:28:32,570
The existence of Sultan
Aladdin is a formality.

284
00:28:34,870 --> 00:28:38,240
İsmihan Sultan is the real danger.

285
00:28:41,800 --> 00:28:44,080
She dreams of reviving a dead country.

286
00:28:47,590 --> 00:28:48,770
İsmihan.

287
00:28:52,510 --> 00:28:54,140
Mother Sultan.

288
00:28:57,070 --> 00:29:00,480
Dozens of foxes roam around her head.

289
00:29:01,950 --> 00:29:05,640
But I will tie all the fox tails together.

290
00:29:07,640 --> 00:29:10,540
And if she makes a mistake...

291
00:29:11,550 --> 00:29:18,140
her son Aladdin will die.

292
00:29:24,670 --> 00:29:29,490
I will destroy her and destroy Osman!

293
00:29:32,670 --> 00:29:35,270
What's going on in your
head, Commander Nayman?

294
00:29:36,150 --> 00:29:38,770
You'll hear about it, it's coming.

295
00:29:53,760 --> 00:29:56,110
The issue is more important
than we expected.

296
00:29:58,230 --> 00:30:00,460
Even the caliph sent us
news of the matter.

297
00:30:01,760 --> 00:30:05,650
Well, is the issue clear
in Muslim countries?

298
00:30:06,300 --> 00:30:07,990
The issue is clear, however...

299
00:30:08,800 --> 00:30:10,810
they ignore it, Osman Bey.

300
00:30:12,640 --> 00:30:16,220
Ghazan Khan's choice of true religion
does not erase the past.

301
00:30:17,170 --> 00:30:23,280
They support Talay, who attacked the
Turkish Beys in the Mamluk state.

302
00:30:23,870 --> 00:30:24,870
Osman Bey.

303
00:30:25,110 --> 00:30:29,020
Some of us have fallen into the
trap of resentment and hatred.

304
00:30:29,790 --> 00:30:31,680
And the rest are
in heedlessness.

305
00:30:31,960 --> 00:30:35,020
And many of us are immersed
in our own interests.

306
00:30:35,960 --> 00:30:37,720
The situation is very serious.

307
00:30:38,720 --> 00:30:41,680
Yes.

308
00:30:42,760 --> 00:30:47,490
There are still people who
stand up for what is right.

309
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:52,370
And there are still those who
did not fall into oblivion.

310
00:30:54,060 --> 00:31:00,890
There are still those who seek
to spread the system around the world.

311
00:31:03,400 --> 00:31:05,370
What are you going to do, Osman Bey?

312
00:31:05,710 --> 00:31:09,850
Will you accept Commander Nayman's offer?
Will you submit to him?

313
00:31:11,150 --> 00:31:16,340
Did you not know that I would accept
this job from the start?

314
00:31:19,840 --> 00:31:22,690
Courage is enough to fight the enemy.

315
00:31:23,670 --> 00:31:30,590
Understanding what is going on in the head of the enemy requires great intelligence, Osman Bey.

316
00:31:31,990 --> 00:31:33,270
What you say is true.

317
00:31:33,940 --> 00:31:34,940
What you say is true.

318
00:31:36,090 --> 00:31:40,350
Thank Allah we have both.

319
00:31:49,740 --> 00:31:51,470
May your war be blessed, Osman Bey.

320
00:31:53,530 --> 00:31:54,660
Thank you.

321
00:31:56,620 --> 00:31:58,860
- May you be safe.
- May you be safe.

322
00:32:44,740 --> 00:32:47,300
Ask forgiveness of Allah and repent to Him.

323
00:32:52,000 --> 00:32:54,140
What is this?

324
00:33:02,880 --> 00:33:06,110
What did your mothers breastfeed you
when you were babies?

325
00:33:15,500 --> 00:33:16,650
Vizier Savelli.

326
00:33:50,590 --> 00:33:51,590
You came.

327
00:33:53,420 --> 00:33:56,150
That's why you survived, merchant.

328
00:33:59,600 --> 00:34:00,970
If you submit to me...

329
00:34:02,040 --> 00:34:06,679
Your entire clan will
survive, not just you.

330
00:34:07,960 --> 00:34:14,389
You will trade all over
the world and not just in this country.

331
00:34:16,840 --> 00:34:18,230
Thank Allah.

332
00:34:20,520 --> 00:34:23,840
I'm basically the biggest
dealer in this country.

333
00:34:27,870 --> 00:34:32,469
Merchant Bayındır is a
good choice, Captain Nayman.

334
00:34:34,179 --> 00:34:37,300
He has a great share in what
Osman made us live in Konya.

335
00:34:42,030 --> 00:34:43,030
I know that.

336
00:34:44,449 --> 00:34:46,050
I know all of this.

337
00:35:09,480 --> 00:35:10,480
And now...

338
00:35:11,830 --> 00:35:18,840
Merchant, you'll turn your back on Osman
and Mother Sultan too.

339
00:35:20,980 --> 00:35:23,190
We have a calling.

340
00:35:24,420 --> 00:35:26,250
Not for a few chests of gold.

341
00:35:30,540 --> 00:35:32,950
Not a few boxes of gold.

342
00:35:33,380 --> 00:35:36,070
And you soul too.

343
00:35:56,550 --> 00:35:58,320
Vizier Savelli.

344
00:35:59,810 --> 00:36:04,760
You set your side from the start,
right?

345
00:36:08,110 --> 00:36:10,980
I'm a smart man, Bayındır.

346
00:36:11,650 --> 00:36:13,770
I recommend this to you too.

347
00:36:17,690 --> 00:36:21,960
The gold that Osman stole from me.

348
00:36:22,680 --> 00:36:26,690
You'll learn all about it first, merchant.

349
00:36:27,540 --> 00:36:33,200
Then, you will tell me every step
Mother Sultan takes and...

350
00:36:33,295 --> 00:36:40,495
everything that goes on between her and Osman.

351
00:37:06,710 --> 00:37:15,090
This is the key that will open
all doors for you, merchant.

352
00:37:19,580 --> 00:37:28,250
Oh my.

353
00:38:01,470 --> 00:38:03,360
Where are you?

354
00:38:05,740 --> 00:38:07,590
Is there no one?

355
00:38:14,350 --> 00:38:15,690
Murat.

356
00:38:17,070 --> 00:38:18,730
Baysungur.

357
00:38:21,300 --> 00:38:22,720
Where are you?

358
00:38:24,460 --> 00:38:26,180
Is there no one?

359
00:38:34,460 --> 00:38:36,500
Where are you?

360
00:38:38,950 --> 00:38:40,890
Ülgen Hatun.

361
00:38:44,320 --> 00:38:46,250
Where is everybody?

362
00:38:47,300 --> 00:38:50,950
They're at war, Cerkutay.
Have you forgotten?

363
00:38:54,450 --> 00:38:56,310
Did we take İnegöl?

364
00:38:56,730 --> 00:38:59,310
Yes, we took it.

365
00:38:59,850 --> 00:39:02,610
Thanks to Gürbüz Alp.

366
00:39:04,460 --> 00:39:05,850
Who?

367
00:39:07,320 --> 00:39:09,480
Is it thanks to Gurbuz Alp?

368
00:39:12,140 --> 00:39:17,200
You opened the door
and I protected you.

369
00:39:18,470 --> 00:39:19,800
What did Gürbüz do?

370
00:39:19,870 --> 00:39:22,340
What did Gürbüz do that we should take
credit for taking the castle to him?

371
00:39:22,760 --> 00:39:24,510
I gave my soul, my soul.

372
00:39:25,280 --> 00:39:26,990
What did Gürbüz do?

373
00:39:28,800 --> 00:39:31,130
Or are you jealous of Gürbüz Alp?

374
00:39:32,590 --> 00:39:35,690
Why would I be jealous of Gürbüz?
What am I going to be jealous of?

375
00:39:35,750 --> 00:39:36,650
Yes.

376
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:40,710
You are jealous, of course.

377
00:39:41,470 --> 00:39:45,040
Gürbüz Alp is very hardworking
and very talented.

378
00:39:45,440 --> 00:39:48,250
He is very brave and strong.

379
00:39:48,720 --> 00:39:51,130
And he eats more food than you.

380
00:39:53,260 --> 00:39:55,460
Since then...

381
00:39:56,100 --> 00:39:59,110
since then...

382
00:40:00,350 --> 00:40:03,130
If Gürbüz Alp does not enter,
you cannot enter the kitchen.

383
00:40:03,570 --> 00:40:05,490
Also, why are you interfering with me?

384
00:40:06,190 --> 00:40:08,580
Don't turn your back on me, Ülgen.

385
00:40:19,900 --> 00:40:21,640
Ülgen.

386
00:40:25,590 --> 00:40:30,260
I.. you.. you..

387
00:40:41,440 --> 00:40:44,660
Cerkutay, did he wake up?

388
00:40:46,070 --> 00:40:47,330
Thank Allah, you woke up!

389
00:40:47,610 --> 00:40:49,400
Praise be to Allah!

390
00:40:52,750 --> 00:40:54,750
He woke up!

391
00:40:55,190 --> 00:40:57,060
He woke up from a very deep dream!

392
00:40:57,290 --> 00:40:59,310
Isn't that right, Cerkutay?

393
00:41:03,770 --> 00:41:05,380
Drink, Cerkutay, drink.

394
00:41:06,060 --> 00:41:09,150
Drink, Cerkutay, drink.

395
00:41:09,670 --> 00:41:11,130
Drink

396
00:41:16,010 --> 00:41:19,190
May your wounds be healed.

397
00:41:21,980 --> 00:41:23,940
Gürbüz.

398
00:41:24,750 --> 00:41:26,120
Get out in front of me.

399
00:41:29,140 --> 00:41:34,750
I'm going to go and tell
Kumral Abdal this good news.

400
00:41:51,290 --> 00:41:53,290
Why are you crying?

401
00:41:54,800 --> 00:41:56,470
I was so afraid, Cerkutay.

402
00:41:57,450 --> 00:42:01,020
I mean, you scared us a lot.

403
00:42:01,530 --> 00:42:04,270
Not only me,
but everyone cried for you.

404
00:42:04,910 --> 00:42:08,270
Especially Boran Alp,
he cried more than me.

405
00:42:20,810 --> 00:42:22,130
You...

406
00:42:23,990 --> 00:42:26,150
Aren't you a brave girl?

407
00:42:27,040 --> 00:42:29,000
I think you aren't afraid.

408
00:42:32,080 --> 00:42:33,740
I am not afraid.

409
00:42:34,860 --> 00:42:36,380
I am not afraid, however...

410
00:42:37,360 --> 00:42:39,440
I am not afraid of the infidels.

411
00:42:42,830 --> 00:42:45,820
I was afraid you might get sick.

412
00:42:47,030 --> 00:42:49,340
Everybody's afraid of this.

413
00:42:55,020 --> 00:42:56,650
Anyway.

414
00:42:58,060 --> 00:43:02,850
I'll bring you soup.

415
00:43:05,700 --> 00:43:07,460
I'll prepare it.

416
00:43:08,560 --> 00:43:10,400
Ülgen.

417
00:43:14,080 --> 00:43:16,100
I got scared too.

418
00:43:18,960 --> 00:43:23,850
I was afraid you wouldn't be able to
get out of that castle alive.

419
00:43:26,320 --> 00:43:31,000
But you got out safe.

420
00:43:45,640 --> 00:43:48,000
I offended you greatly.

421
00:43:50,780 --> 00:43:53,390
My brother's life is safe.

422
00:43:57,240 --> 00:43:59,870
Punish me.

423
00:44:00,910 --> 00:44:02,800
I accept everything you say.

424
00:44:06,250 --> 00:44:11,250
Since you said this, you know
what your actions caused.

425
00:44:11,940 --> 00:44:13,320
Isn't that right, Esma?

426
00:44:13,690 --> 00:44:14,880
I know.

427
00:44:16,770 --> 00:44:19,010
I am ashamed to ask for forgiveness.

428
00:44:21,950 --> 00:44:26,650
There is no pardon for what I have done,
I accept any punishment you decide.

429
00:44:40,740 --> 00:44:46,050
If only I hadn't known that you made
this mistake for your brother's life...

430
00:44:46,860 --> 00:44:50,270
I would have killed you the day I
learned of your betrayal.

431
00:44:52,160 --> 00:44:54,900
You're right, Malhun Hatun.

432
00:45:05,710 --> 00:45:07,790
And now you will promise me.

433
00:45:08,140 --> 00:45:10,280
You will never make such a mistake again.

434
00:45:10,560 --> 00:45:11,940
I won't.

435
00:45:13,850 --> 00:45:15,280
I will never do this again.

436
00:45:17,420 --> 00:45:19,470
I learned my lesson.

437
00:45:20,920 --> 00:45:22,840
I did so many bad things.

438
00:45:27,490 --> 00:45:29,620
Punish me.

439
00:45:31,730 --> 00:45:34,620
Punish me now so that it does
not remain for the hereafter.

440
00:45:39,530 --> 00:45:42,680
I forgive you for my right, Esma.

441
00:45:43,890 --> 00:45:45,890
You are not going anywhere.

442
00:45:46,480 --> 00:45:50,490
You will pay for what you did
by living here with us.

443
00:45:57,790 --> 00:46:00,080
I promise, Malhun Hatun.

444
00:46:00,720 --> 00:46:02,150
I promise you.

445
00:46:07,470 --> 00:46:10,430
I will protect your children
even if it costs me my life.

446
00:46:12,890 --> 00:46:15,360
I will get you right one day.

447
00:46:37,010 --> 00:46:39,270
Tell me, how are the preparations?

448
00:46:39,810 --> 00:46:41,650
The preparations are
complete, Osman Bey.

449
00:46:41,720 --> 00:46:44,330
We are ready, very ready.

450
00:46:51,250 --> 00:46:54,250
So say quick, we don't
have much time.

451
00:46:54,470 --> 00:46:59,770
You go alone to
the hole of the foxes we want to kill.

452
00:47:00,700 --> 00:47:02,180
Don't.

453
00:47:04,330 --> 00:47:06,490
All the holes in this country are ours.

454
00:47:06,930 --> 00:47:09,860
The uninvited guest is Nayman.

455
00:47:12,020 --> 00:47:15,200
Either he will die or he will be gone.

456
00:47:17,220 --> 00:47:19,120
We are not going to give up.

457
00:47:19,420 --> 00:47:21,690
We go to receive and take.

458
00:47:21,760 --> 00:47:22,870
Inshallah.

459
00:47:23,110 --> 00:47:25,990
- Inshallah, my Bey.
- Inshallah.

460
00:47:26,660 --> 00:47:29,130
Nevertheless, take care of
yourself.

461
00:47:29,700 --> 00:47:33,790
At the slightest mistake, the place of the
hunter and the prey change, Osman Bey.

462
00:47:34,090 --> 00:47:36,110
What do we do next?

463
00:47:36,450 --> 00:47:39,170
So, we won't make ay mistake.

464
00:47:39,750 --> 00:47:41,910
We won't.

465
00:47:42,620 --> 00:47:44,470
It's time.

466
00:47:45,120 --> 00:47:47,450
Release the captives.

467
00:47:48,670 --> 00:47:49,810
Your command, my Bey.

468
00:47:49,850 --> 00:47:51,320
Your command, my Bey.

469
00:47:51,970 --> 00:47:53,120
Turgut.

470
00:47:54,290 --> 00:47:59,370
In my absence, the estates and warriors
who are at my command...

471
00:48:00,450 --> 00:48:01,470
will be your lead.

472
00:48:02,530 --> 00:48:04,810
Your words will echo on my sword.

473
00:48:05,530 --> 00:48:08,800
We'll be where
you said it at the time you said it.

474
00:48:10,770 --> 00:48:12,600
Everything will go as
we would like, Inshallah.

475
00:48:12,650 --> 00:48:13,460
Inshallah.

476
00:48:15,330 --> 00:48:18,100
Inshallah.

477
00:48:19,160 --> 00:48:20,180
Give me your blessings.

478
00:48:20,210 --> 00:48:22,090
- We give you blessings, my Bey.
- We give you blessings, my Bey.

479
00:48:22,340 --> 00:48:23,990
We give you blessings, my Bey.

480
00:48:24,370 --> 00:48:26,330
We give you blessings, my Bey.

481
00:48:27,430 --> 00:48:28,960
Give us your blessings, my Bey.

482
00:48:30,160 --> 00:48:32,370
I give you blessings.

483
00:48:32,690 --> 00:48:35,360
Take care of yourself.

484
00:48:36,310 --> 00:48:38,290
We still have a lot of
work to do.

485
00:48:40,860 --> 00:48:42,550
Let's get over this first.

486
00:48:43,200 --> 00:48:44,600
We'll get thorugh this.

487
00:48:45,050 --> 00:48:46,180
We'll look at the rest.

488
00:48:46,620 --> 00:48:47,940
Hear me now well.

489
00:48:50,720 --> 00:48:53,970
The merchant will bring what we ask.

490
00:48:54,710 --> 00:48:59,830
And you shall become a
viper in this region, Savelli.

491
00:49:01,080 --> 00:49:02,710
Your command, Commander Nayman.

492
00:49:07,380 --> 00:49:10,890
İsmihan will think that you
are on her side.

493
00:49:11,700 --> 00:49:16,610
You will complete what the merchant lacks.

494
00:49:18,350 --> 00:49:20,460
We'll make a big fire.

495
00:49:20,930 --> 00:49:25,110
You will burn the enemy
and we'll warm our people.

496
00:49:26,950 --> 00:49:31,250
Go get wood for that fire.

497
00:49:31,570 --> 00:49:33,080
Let's go.

498
00:49:41,810 --> 00:49:43,690
You will target the convoy first.

499
00:49:44,290 --> 00:49:46,320
This will be your first campaign.

500
00:49:47,090 --> 00:49:49,920
You'll get news after I say it.

501
00:49:50,850 --> 00:49:54,600
I'll tell Nayman that there is a spark of
disobedience within the army...

502
00:49:54,710 --> 00:49:57,110
and it will flare up.

503
00:49:57,190 --> 00:50:02,850
Then the soldiers will enter, who
will say that Nayman has chosen Islam.

504
00:50:03,240 --> 00:50:04,480
You will release them.

505
00:50:07,110 --> 00:50:08,290
My Bey.

506
00:50:08,830 --> 00:50:11,220
Aren't these the Muslim army
of Ghazan Khan?

507
00:50:12,270 --> 00:50:14,080
Why do they oppose our religion?

508
00:50:14,520 --> 00:50:15,420
No.

509
00:50:16,430 --> 00:50:18,510
These are the opponents of Ghazan Khan.

510
00:50:19,160 --> 00:50:22,400
They are the ones who want to erase
Islam from these lands.

511
00:50:23,940 --> 00:50:26,160
When they hear that
Nayman has chosen Islam...

512
00:50:26,920 --> 00:50:28,720
They will think he has been deceived.

513
00:50:31,840 --> 00:50:33,470
And the disobedience will begin.

514
00:50:35,960 --> 00:50:36,850
Then?

515
00:50:38,340 --> 00:50:40,270
When it appears that
what I've said is true...

516
00:50:40,340 --> 00:50:42,730
Nayman will trust me completely.

517
00:50:44,550 --> 00:50:46,510
He'll think I'm defending him.

518
00:50:48,800 --> 00:50:50,520
And then, the main topic...

519
00:50:51,300 --> 00:50:56,150
He will tell me which country campaigns
he would like to establish one by one...

520
00:50:58,380 --> 00:51:02,340
Those who want to know
the truth will walk to the fire.

521
00:51:03,220 --> 00:51:07,430
And the secret of the fire
is for those who enter the fire only.

522
00:51:10,480 --> 00:51:11,410
Thank you.

523
00:51:24,340 --> 00:51:33,110
Let's see if Osman
and İsmihan will burn or warm.

524
00:51:35,780 --> 00:51:36,830
Gök Talay.

525
00:51:38,790 --> 00:51:44,370
Let the soldiers go out
and welcome the oncoming caravan.

526
00:51:47,740 --> 00:51:48,950
Great Commander Nayman.

527
00:51:49,280 --> 00:51:50,240
Come here.

528
00:51:57,300 --> 00:51:59,850
Osman Bey is coming.

529
00:52:04,690 --> 00:52:05,500
Let him come.

530
00:52:39,230 --> 00:52:41,310
You will die Osman, you will die.

531
00:52:41,770 --> 00:52:45,120
- You will die, Osman.
- You will die, Osman.

532
00:52:45,300 --> 00:52:46,910
You will die.

533
00:52:51,900 --> 00:52:54,540
- You will die.
- you will die.

534
00:53:07,740 --> 00:53:10,750
You will die Osman, you will die.

535
00:53:51,380 --> 00:53:53,410
Is that
possible, mother?

536
00:53:53,780 --> 00:53:55,570
We buried Öktem Bey yesterday.

537
00:53:56,120 --> 00:53:57,090
What will people say?

538
00:53:58,150 --> 00:53:59,630
Son, we said, we said that too.

539
00:53:59,870 --> 00:54:02,650
However, she doesn't listen.

540
00:54:02,960 --> 00:54:05,330
She says, if you don't
have a wedding...

541
00:54:05,770 --> 00:54:07,950
she will break the engagement.

542
00:54:16,530 --> 00:54:18,090
What does thisHatun want to do?

543
00:54:18,430 --> 00:54:19,830
What are you seeking again?

544
00:54:20,390 --> 00:54:22,430
Something comes
to my mind, however...

545
00:54:22,530 --> 00:54:24,640
Are you thinking what I'm thinking, Bala?

546
00:54:27,870 --> 00:54:29,890
What do you think
Bengi Hatun thinks?

547
00:54:30,180 --> 00:54:32,290
Öktem Bey doesn't have a son, does he?

548
00:54:34,810 --> 00:54:39,080
Bengi Hatun sat on the throne today, but
Beys will not remain silent about this situation.

549
00:54:39,780 --> 00:54:41,810
- She would like...
- Mother.

550
00:54:44,040 --> 00:54:44,890
Sons.

551
00:54:47,070 --> 00:54:48,480
Let your path be open.

552
00:54:48,520 --> 00:54:49,760
Thank you.

553
00:54:52,230 --> 00:54:56,240
Take care of each other.

554
00:54:56,310 --> 00:54:57,500
Be careful, okay?

555
00:55:01,970 --> 00:55:03,270
Let's go.

556
00:55:03,620 --> 00:55:07,890
Let's distribute the gold that the people
deserve and lighten the burden on our backs.

557
00:55:09,090 --> 00:55:09,840
Let's go.

558
00:55:09,870 --> 00:55:12,400
Warriors, warriors, come on to the horses.

559
00:55:16,470 --> 00:55:19,060
Let's go.

560
00:55:20,120 --> 00:55:22,990
Let's go.

561
00:55:44,980 --> 00:55:50,570
Did Osman say his decision
so that we hasten to his sword?

562
00:55:53,580 --> 00:55:55,630
Osman will say his decision.

563
00:55:57,510 --> 00:56:02,430
Then we will know if his
sword is at our service.

564
00:56:03,050 --> 00:56:05,760
Or is our sword on his neck?

565
00:56:06,280 --> 00:56:08,860
My sword...

566
00:56:09,360 --> 00:56:11,480
services my Allah only.

567
00:56:14,330 --> 00:56:16,240
My Allah says to me, protect
your people.

568
00:56:18,700 --> 00:56:20,470
The way to protect my people...

569
00:56:23,060 --> 00:56:24,400
passes through you.

570
00:56:25,970 --> 00:56:27,150
But...

571
00:56:29,340 --> 00:56:32,310
Don't think I'm afraid
because your sword is on my neck.

572
00:56:32,900 --> 00:56:38,020
If you would have been afraid, I would not
have wanted you in my army, Osman.

573
00:56:39,650 --> 00:56:43,590
You are a brave man who
thinks of his people.

574
00:56:44,820 --> 00:56:47,600
This is the thing that
keeps you alive.

575
00:56:51,080 --> 00:56:54,660
Don't forget, cowards die every day.

576
00:56:55,410 --> 00:56:57,330
And the brave die once.

577
00:56:59,140 --> 00:57:04,220
But I would like all my soldiers
to hear your loyalty

578
00:57:06,350 --> 00:57:09,930
So that
no one shall be disrespectful again.

579
00:57:12,420 --> 00:57:13,930
Say Osman.

580
00:57:21,570 --> 00:57:22,390
I

581
00:57:24,780 --> 00:57:25,790
The Bey of Kayis.

582
00:57:28,010 --> 00:57:30,750
The owner of all the properties
in the border areas, Osman Bey.

583
00:57:33,470 --> 00:57:34,690
My sword...

584
00:57:38,600 --> 00:57:40,720
...is at the service of commander Nayman.

585
00:57:42,110 --> 00:57:46,400
My life depends on his words
and my moves are with his commands.

586
00:57:47,790 --> 00:57:50,040
Even I hardly heard you.

587
00:57:51,630 --> 00:57:52,860
Repeat Osman!

588
00:58:09,710 --> 00:58:10,830
From now on...

589
00:58:15,970 --> 00:58:16,870
My sword...

590
00:58:20,800 --> 00:58:23,120
...is at the service of commander Nayman!

591
00:58:34,020 --> 00:58:35,110
Keep it.

592
00:58:38,380 --> 00:58:46,030
Do you know why I did not kill you and
wanted you to be under my command, Osman?

593
00:58:48,380 --> 00:58:49,060
Say.

594
00:58:50,030 --> 00:58:54,550
Because you have no equal.

595
00:58:55,450 --> 00:59:00,970
Otherwise, I would have killed
you on the first day.

596
00:59:05,020 --> 00:59:09,200
Let's go into the tent.
I have a lot to ask

597
00:59:45,990 --> 00:59:46,920
They are coming

598
00:59:51,660 --> 00:59:53,240
Prepare your fishook, Boran

599
00:59:54,350 --> 00:59:56,040
We'll fish today.

600
01:00:08,950 --> 01:00:09,880
Be vigilant.

601
01:00:16,370 --> 01:00:20,250
The goods and weapons in this upcoming
caravan are very important to Nayman.

602
01:00:21,800 --> 01:00:24,590
If we manage take them,
we will severely break their power.

603
01:00:25,560 --> 01:00:31,680
The more we sieze his ammunation,
the greater we hit him.

604
01:00:32,640 --> 01:00:35,120
I hope so, Turgut Bey, I hope so.

605
01:00:40,540 --> 01:00:41,920
Now!

606
01:00:42,560 --> 01:00:44,880
Oh right!

607
01:02:52,500 --> 01:02:53,900
Table!

608
01:03:55,480 --> 01:03:56,900
Osman!

609
01:03:58,340 --> 01:04:00,900
This lamb was bred in a special way.

610
01:04:00,900 --> 01:04:06,020
Only the toughest warriors deserve it.

611
01:04:10,140 --> 01:04:12,820
Thank you, thank you.

612
01:04:14,260 --> 01:04:16,420
You're so honored, Nayman.

613
01:04:16,620 --> 01:04:17,940
Help yourself

614
01:04:22,080 --> 01:04:23,760
Don't worry

615
01:04:24,520 --> 01:04:27,000
I made the Muslim butchers slaughter it.

616
01:04:32,700 --> 01:04:33,680
Thank you.

617
01:04:36,720 --> 01:04:37,800
Thank you.

618
01:04:40,460 --> 01:04:42,060
In the name of Allah,
the most gracious, the most merciful

619
01:04:47,440 --> 01:04:48,740
Well, tell me.

620
01:04:51,400 --> 01:04:54,340
Is me being a Muslim a problem for you?

621
01:04:54,340 --> 01:05:01,000
An obedient Muslim is not a problem for me

622
01:05:01,540 --> 01:05:03,000
Well, what about Ghazan Khan?

623
01:05:04,380 --> 01:05:06,500
A Muslim is the ruler of the state.

624
01:05:07,300 --> 01:05:09,220
Is that a problem for you?

625
01:05:11,380 --> 01:05:14,400
Whoever is under
my command can be a Muslim.

626
01:05:14,400 --> 01:05:17,060
But he who is in a higher position than me,
can never.

627
01:05:18,160 --> 01:05:23,860
Ghazan Khan made a choice,
and he will pay for it

628
01:05:23,860 --> 01:05:29,860
And what about you?
You are serving a non-Muslim person.

629
01:05:30,420 --> 01:05:33,080
Will this bother you?

630
01:05:38,400 --> 01:05:41,640
My only goal is the people of my tribe.

631
01:05:43,800 --> 01:05:49,780
I serve whomever I ought to serve
for their sake..

632
01:05:52,560 --> 01:05:53,820
Well, you say.

633
01:05:55,040 --> 01:05:56,720
What is your purpose?

634
01:05:58,340 --> 01:05:59,820
What will you do with Ghazan Khan?

635
01:06:01,580 --> 01:06:03,980
It is enough for us to part ways now.

636
01:06:05,700 --> 01:06:07,620
I will draw my own path.

637
01:06:07,980 --> 01:06:12,340
I see that road will lead to a state.

638
01:06:13,580 --> 01:06:15,780
I will found a state, Osman

639
01:06:23,700 --> 01:06:25,300
A state, huh?

640
01:06:29,120 --> 01:06:31,200
State issue is a huge issue.

641
01:06:32,720 --> 01:06:33,720
So...

642
01:06:36,220 --> 01:06:37,580
How will you do that?

643
01:06:40,040 --> 01:06:43,460
Strength lies in weapons and gold.

644
01:06:44,530 --> 01:06:46,830
There are caravans coming to me right now.

645
01:06:47,271 --> 01:06:51,650
Caravans that carry weapon and gold to me.

646
01:06:51,650 --> 01:06:51,731
They will make me stronger here.
Caravans that carry weapon and gold to me.

647
01:06:51,731 --> 01:06:55,310
They will make me stronger here.

648
01:06:55,770 --> 01:06:59,010
And I will create a state with that power.

649
01:06:59,010 --> 01:07:01,510
Well, will we have our share of the gold?

650
01:07:02,870 --> 01:07:05,370
You just need to be loyal to me, Osman.

651
01:07:05,750 --> 01:07:11,490
Just serve to me and both glory
and gold shall be yours.

652
01:07:11,490 --> 01:07:13,490
Eyvallah, Eyvallah.
(Thank you)

653
01:07:14,010 --> 01:07:16,030
So, as a first service to you...

654
01:07:18,650 --> 01:07:21,710
Let me warn you.

655
01:07:23,790 --> 01:07:25,810
Those tribes won't listen to you.

656
01:07:26,790 --> 01:07:29,010
And they will attack your caravan.

657
01:07:30,290 --> 01:07:31,810
This is how it happens here.

658
01:07:32,630 --> 01:07:34,210
Not safe at all.

659
01:07:35,430 --> 01:07:37,270
They will attack the caravan.

660
01:07:37,650 --> 01:07:40,170
No one can dare to do that, Osman.

661
01:07:41,150 --> 01:07:43,950
Eyvallah (okay).
Whatever you think.

662
01:08:32,189 --> 01:08:34,970
Now Nayman has taken the major hit.

663
01:09:06,430 --> 01:09:08,330
Good for you alps.

664
01:09:08,830 --> 01:09:12,970
The prey we caught turned out to be
bigger than we expected

665
01:09:15,569 --> 01:09:16,859
What is it, Turgut Bey?

666
01:09:17,670 --> 01:09:21,828
This is the map of the route of caravans.

667
01:09:22,450 --> 01:09:25,209
It marks the places where Nayman's
caravans are waiting.

668
01:09:25,209 --> 01:09:29,209
We are going to find them so easily.

669
01:09:29,209 --> 01:09:31,209
We will destroy them all.

670
01:09:31,209 --> 01:09:32,910
Oi Masha Allah!

671
01:09:33,209 --> 01:09:35,010
Tell me, Turgut Bey.

672
01:09:35,109 --> 01:09:38,328
We asked for an eye, Lord gave us two.

673
01:09:43,550 --> 01:09:45,709
Such an unfortuneate, Kutan!

674
01:09:46,649 --> 01:09:48,189
Turgut Bey.

675
01:09:48,550 --> 01:09:51,390
Let's knit a dress for Nayman
out of this silk.

676
01:09:52,550 --> 01:09:56,130
Alright, Boran.
You are in your merciful day.

677
01:10:02,410 --> 01:10:03,910
...but, my Bey...

678
01:10:04,230 --> 01:10:06,750
Isn't silk forbidden for men?

679
01:10:07,170 --> 01:10:11,250
Forbidden for men,
not for that dishonorable Nayman.

680
01:10:15,210 --> 01:10:17,710
Nayman must be regretting
about how wrong he was!

681
01:10:20,470 --> 01:10:21,790
Eyvallah!

682
01:10:22,410 --> 01:10:24,470
Osman Bey's game has succeeded

683
01:10:25,350 --> 01:10:27,370
But this is still just the beginning.

684
01:10:27,370 --> 01:10:29,370
We're not even halfway there.

685
01:10:29,370 --> 01:10:34,330
We will distribute the goods
to the people now.

686
01:10:36,610 --> 01:10:38,350
Come on, let's go

687
01:10:55,765 --> 01:10:58,765
Sogut.

688
01:10:59,190 --> 01:11:01,010
You're late, Bayindir.

689
01:11:01,010 --> 01:11:02,710
Where have you been?

690
01:11:03,775 --> 01:11:06,635
Forgive me, Mother Sultan.

691
01:11:06,635 --> 01:11:07,955
You are right

692
01:11:07,955 --> 01:11:13,135
...but you know, I've been away from
commerce for a long time

693
01:11:13,135 --> 01:11:18,155
I said let's go out and
check out my stores.

694
01:11:19,455 --> 01:11:20,955
Future is uncertain.

695
01:11:20,955 --> 01:11:24,835
We don't know when
it might occur to Osman Bey...

696
01:11:24,835 --> 01:11:27,675
...and he decides to
shut down my stores!

697
01:11:27,675 --> 01:11:29,695
Can't he do that?
Maybe.

698
01:11:30,515 --> 01:11:33,215
He wouldn't, Bayindir.

699
01:11:35,255 --> 01:11:37,675
Osman Bey and I
are in the same side now

700
01:11:38,315 --> 01:11:41,355
The more you earn he will earn too.

701
01:11:42,675 --> 01:11:45,615
You know what's best.

702
01:11:46,575 --> 01:11:50,035
You have a point in the present time,
Mother Sultan.

703
01:11:50,675 --> 01:11:54,435
But only Allah alone can know the future.

704
01:11:54,795 --> 01:11:57,515
Until yesterday, you and Osman Bey
were staunch enemies

705
01:11:59,145 --> 01:12:00,775
However, today...

706
01:12:01,355 --> 01:12:05,395
Like I said, you know what's best.

707
01:12:06,135 --> 01:12:09,135
If you say we are friends, we are.

708
01:12:09,135 --> 01:12:13,715
If I say we are enemies,
I will sharpen my sword for them.

709
01:12:18,475 --> 01:12:22,955
Nayman won't stop after cutting
Oktem Bey's head, Bayindir.

710
01:12:24,335 --> 01:12:26,605
If we side with Nayman...

711
01:12:26,875 --> 01:12:29,105
We will lose all the Turkmen tribes.

712
01:12:32,465 --> 01:12:34,585
If we side with Osman Bey's side...

713
01:12:35,145 --> 01:12:37,715
We'll both be good with Turkmens and...

714
01:12:38,125 --> 01:12:42,505
We'll have a chance to get rid of Nayman.

715
01:12:43,545 --> 01:12:48,835
Dear Mother Sultan, who is Osman Bey?

716
01:12:49,165 --> 01:12:55,035
Who is he to unite with us
and remove Nayman?

717
01:12:57,095 --> 01:12:59,705
Still, you know the best.

718
01:12:59,705 --> 01:13:03,045
I am thinking about the gold.

719
01:13:03,045 --> 01:13:07,035
The gold that Osman Bey took from
the rest of the Beys.

720
01:13:07,635 --> 01:13:09,765
The gold has not been found yet.

721
01:13:11,415 --> 01:13:14,485
Osman Bey must have a plan.

722
01:13:14,935 --> 01:13:17,795
Forget about the gold now.

723
01:13:18,225 --> 01:13:25,755
Go to our people and fulfill their needs
in the name of Mother Sultan.

724
01:13:27,325 --> 01:13:30,865
As you order, Mother Sultan.

725
01:13:46,805 --> 01:13:50,295
Bayindir's mind is clouded, Celali.

726
01:13:54,575 --> 01:13:56,295
I don't trust him.

727
01:13:57,065 --> 01:14:00,615
Tell me about every step he takes.

728
01:14:01,125 --> 01:14:04,225
As you command, Mother Sultan.

729
01:14:08,385 --> 01:14:10,175
Mother Sultan.

730
01:14:11,545 --> 01:14:12,865
My Bey!

731
01:14:13,095 --> 01:14:16,905
She was going to kill me!
She was about to kill me!

732
01:14:17,395 --> 01:14:21,035
Why?
Because I cooperated with Osman Bey!

733
01:14:21,315 --> 01:14:23,055
What has changed now?

734
01:14:23,915 --> 01:14:25,505
Who am I?

735
01:14:25,695 --> 01:14:28,605
She is telling me to side with Osman Bey!

736
01:14:28,815 --> 01:14:32,005
Her face doesn't even go red!

737
01:14:32,820 --> 01:14:34,680
You are right, my Bey.

738
01:14:34,900 --> 01:14:36,710
Yet I have an important news.

739
01:14:37,470 --> 01:14:38,990
Say.

740
01:14:41,290 --> 01:14:46,000
Aktemur and Hatuns
departed to hand out the gold.

741
01:14:47,080 --> 01:14:48,650
Yes, just like that.

742
01:14:49,890 --> 01:14:52,650
Osman Bey is the sign of justice.

743
01:14:53,000 --> 01:14:55,510
He will definitely share the gold.

744
01:14:55,890 --> 01:14:58,080
Good, good.

745
01:14:58,850 --> 01:15:01,470
We'll go after the gold at once!

746
01:15:02,880 --> 01:15:05,670
We act according to our interests, Huseyin.
We'll work for ourselves.

747
01:15:06,050 --> 01:15:10,320
We will work for ourselves.
Only for ourselves.

748
01:15:12,630 --> 01:15:14,360
Let's go Huseyin.

749
01:15:18,165 --> 01:15:20,215
Commander Neyman

750
01:15:23,445 --> 01:15:26,685
The caravan has been attacked.

751
01:15:38,165 --> 01:15:41,105
How did you see it coming, Osman?

752
01:15:42,075 --> 01:15:44,645
This land is my home, Nayman.

753
01:15:45,635 --> 01:15:47,145
I told you.

754
01:15:47,605 --> 01:15:49,975
I'm the one who knows the best here.

755
01:15:50,475 --> 01:15:53,035
You can think like this:

756
01:15:54,965 --> 01:15:57,115
A caravan of yours was attacked.

757
01:15:58,255 --> 01:16:03,655
But you gained a commander who saw in advance
that the caravan would be attacked.

758
01:16:04,735 --> 01:16:06,715
If you cooperate with me...

759
01:16:08,005 --> 01:16:10,675
You will earn ten times as much.

760
01:16:14,715 --> 01:16:16,225
You are right.

761
01:16:16,635 --> 01:16:20,665
A caravan goes, a caravan comes.
But I now have Osman!

762
01:16:20,775 --> 01:16:22,865
Exactly.

763
01:16:24,725 --> 01:16:30,035
We were talking about the state
before the caravan issue.

764
01:16:30,145 --> 01:16:31,765
Tell me now.

765
01:16:35,545 --> 01:16:39,255
You talk about gold and weapon.

766
01:16:39,435 --> 01:16:41,505
But you need to be men for these.

767
01:16:42,095 --> 01:16:45,395
You need number.
What's your plan here?

768
01:16:46,615 --> 01:16:51,685
You understand the affairs of this country,
don't you, Osman?

769
01:16:52,885 --> 01:16:57,585
We thought about this and
performed our campaign.

770
01:16:58,495 --> 01:17:02,595
I'll collect Muslim children from the tribes.

771
01:17:03,465 --> 01:17:06,065
They will be raised for me.

772
01:17:06,635 --> 01:17:09,375
They will serve me.

773
01:17:11,255 --> 01:17:14,695
Doesn't that bother you?

774
01:17:22,425 --> 01:17:28,485
As long as you don't touch my tribe,
it's not a problem for me.

775
01:17:29,755 --> 01:17:31,375
I said this before too.

776
01:17:31,945 --> 01:17:35,225
Whoever does not side with me is against me.

777
01:17:37,065 --> 01:17:39,395
From now on, everyone will walk alone.

778
01:17:52,455 --> 01:17:54,665
Osman.

779
01:17:58,835 --> 01:18:01,325
Osman, Osman.

780
01:18:02,435 --> 01:18:06,135
We will do very big business together.

781
01:18:06,865 --> 01:18:10,875
History will talk about us forever!

782
01:18:11,665 --> 01:18:14,215
Will you found this country alone?

783
01:18:14,615 --> 01:18:17,205
I have you!

784
01:18:19,205 --> 01:18:22,865
Eyvallah, (thank you)you consider
us on your way. That makes me happy.

785
01:18:24,675 --> 01:18:26,705
But I am not talking about that.

786
01:18:29,355 --> 01:18:31,395
Do you have a brother behind you?

787
01:18:32,785 --> 01:18:35,525
Or a friend? I'm talking about this.

788
01:18:37,525 --> 01:18:40,405
Are you trying to imply something?

789
01:18:41,515 --> 01:18:43,705
Since we will walk together...

790
01:18:44,635 --> 01:18:46,495
Since I will protect you...

791
01:18:47,945 --> 01:18:51,005
I want to know if
there's someone who supports you.

792
01:18:51,005 --> 01:18:53,285
You ask a lot of questions, Osman.

793
01:18:53,595 --> 01:18:56,255
That's enough for you now.

794
01:18:59,705 --> 01:19:04,345
Alright then,
let's get over with the questions.

795
01:19:06,145 --> 01:19:08,495
I have another warning for you.

796
01:19:12,905 --> 01:19:15,375
According to the news I received.

797
01:19:18,235 --> 01:19:21,795
There is a preparation to rebel against you
in the army.

798
01:19:25,435 --> 01:19:27,365
What is your tongue saying, Osman?!

799
01:19:27,365 --> 01:19:29,035
The truth!

800
01:19:31,055 --> 01:19:32,645
The truth.

801
01:19:36,635 --> 01:19:39,035
You still don't know my army yet.

802
01:19:39,445 --> 01:19:41,315
You will get to know now.

803
01:19:43,425 --> 01:19:45,385
Let the Majors come.

804
01:20:20,035 --> 01:20:22,255
This road takes us to their hole, brother.

805
01:20:22,815 --> 01:20:24,645
You're right, Aykurt.

806
01:20:26,025 --> 01:20:29,305
Since they're rushing to Nayman...

807
01:20:29,525 --> 01:20:31,595
This means that they suspected something.

808
01:20:35,715 --> 01:20:37,635
They must have.

809
01:20:38,035 --> 01:20:41,745
This suspicion will cause discord
in Nayman's army.

810
01:21:23,945 --> 01:21:27,095
Come on, there's nothing,
let's get back to the headquarters.

811
01:21:27,535 --> 01:21:29,215
Nayman will answer to the soldiers.

812
01:21:29,215 --> 01:21:31,775
He betrayed Tengri
(Turkish-Mongolian God)

813
01:21:41,805 --> 01:21:44,145
Osman Bey's plan is going well, Aykurt

814
01:21:44,585 --> 01:21:45,935
Let's go.

815
01:22:13,215 --> 01:22:14,725
Alps!

816
01:22:31,505 --> 01:22:33,575
Who are you_

817
01:22:33,575 --> 01:22:35,155
Are you from the Kayi tribe?

818
01:22:35,265 --> 01:22:37,015
We are from the family of Osman Bey.

819
01:22:37,015 --> 01:22:38,725
Say, what is the reason you hurry?

820
01:22:38,725 --> 01:22:42,885
The Mongol soldiers collect children from the
Turkmen tribes in order to raise them.

821
01:22:43,125 --> 01:22:44,835
They entered the nearby tribes.

822
01:22:45,235 --> 01:22:48,275
What are you saying?
Where are they now?

823
01:22:48,275 --> 01:22:50,925
Wesent several alps behind their caravan.

824
01:22:50,975 --> 01:22:53,215
Part of them went to neighboring tribes.

825
01:22:53,485 --> 01:22:55,015
But their number is very large.

826
01:22:55,015 --> 01:22:57,195
We can do nothing alone.

827
01:22:57,385 --> 01:22:59,355
We need help.

828
01:23:04,075 --> 01:23:05,555
Aktemur.

829
01:23:05,695 --> 01:23:09,265
You deliver the gold,
we go after those dogs.

830
01:23:09,265 --> 01:23:11,825
Let the alps go with you.
We will take care of ourselves.

831
01:23:11,825 --> 01:23:12,945
Not possible.

832
01:23:12,995 --> 01:23:14,385
Gold is important.

833
01:23:14,385 --> 01:23:17,245
It should be distributed to the people
without any problems.

834
01:23:17,245 --> 01:23:19,135
We will take care of ourselves.

835
01:23:19,715 --> 01:23:20,985
Son!

836
01:23:21,355 --> 01:23:24,125
When your work is done, you will join us.

837
01:23:24,125 --> 01:23:25,425
Come on.

838
01:23:26,305 --> 01:23:27,665
Eyvallah (Okay)

839
01:23:27,845 --> 01:23:30,435
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

840
01:23:34,365 --> 01:23:35,725
Alps!

841
01:23:35,775 --> 01:23:37,135
Let'S go.

842
01:23:55,065 --> 01:23:57,355
What shall we do now, my Bey?

843
01:23:57,825 --> 01:23:59,405
They are splitting.

844
01:24:00,385 --> 01:24:02,105
Don't you know, Huseyin.

845
01:24:03,265 --> 01:24:07,135
Our only goal is gold.

846
01:24:07,675 --> 01:24:12,025
We can get by for the rest of our lives with it.

847
01:24:12,475 --> 01:24:15,445
We'll go after Aktemur.

848
01:24:16,225 --> 01:24:18,025
Your command, my Bey.

849
01:24:18,455 --> 01:24:22,515
Also, I have an account with Aktemur that
I haven't settled yet.

850
01:24:23,025 --> 01:24:29,065
When he dies while sharing the gold,
nobody will suspect me.

851
01:24:30,055 --> 01:24:31,415
Let's go.

852
01:24:35,415 --> 01:24:42,815
We hit the caravan and not only hit it,
we struck fear into Nayman's heart as well.

853
01:24:45,505 --> 01:24:51,185
Osman Bey told us to attack the caravan
and we did it. Mission accomplished, Turgut Bey.

854
01:24:51,415 --> 01:24:53,995
Yes, we have been successful, thank Allah.

855
01:24:55,955 --> 01:24:58,455
What do we do next, Turgut Bey?

856
01:25:01,335 --> 01:25:03,925
Those valiants will tell us what's next.

857
01:25:14,375 --> 01:25:16,255
Peace be upon you.

858
01:25:16,295 --> 01:25:17,645
And may peace be upon you too.

859
01:25:17,695 --> 01:25:19,015
Tell me.

860
01:25:19,035 --> 01:25:23,235
We did what you told us, Turgut Bey,
we released the two Mongol soldiers at Inegol.

861
01:25:23,305 --> 01:25:24,685
Eyvallah (thank you)

862
01:25:25,305 --> 01:25:29,685
Well, do you think they were convinced
that Nayman had the honor of converting to Islam?

863
01:25:30,105 --> 01:25:34,695
They will forget their horses, but they will never
forget what Nayman did, Turgut Bey.

864
01:25:38,395 --> 01:25:40,355
Were they angry?

865
01:25:40,605 --> 01:25:43,915
Their fear outweighted their anger...

866
01:25:43,915 --> 01:25:48,055
but after they enter the army headquarters,
their anger will outweight their fear.

867
01:25:48,315 --> 01:25:51,075
Then the rebellion will break out
in the army headquarters, huh?

868
01:25:52,665 --> 01:25:56,755
Osman Bey managed the toughest challange.

869
01:25:59,485 --> 01:26:01,295
Thank Allah.

870
01:26:11,455 --> 01:26:18,215
Majors! Osman says there are
rebellious voices within my army.

871
01:26:18,705 --> 01:26:21,985
Each and every Mongol soldiers
are loyal to Nayman.

872
01:26:22,225 --> 01:26:27,225
This army was made up of believers only,
there are no cracks in the army, Nayman.

873
01:26:34,735 --> 01:26:39,205
You claim that your Majors control
every single Mongol soldier in their troop.

874
01:26:40,135 --> 01:26:46,195
You claim that they know each one of them
and control each one of them, is that true?

875
01:26:46,655 --> 01:26:49,925
Do you doubt their loyalty?

876
01:26:51,985 --> 01:26:53,625
Then tell me.

877
01:26:55,955 --> 01:26:58,255
If Ghazan Khan sent you a letter...

878
01:26:58,795 --> 01:27:02,915
...and told you to leave the army,
what would you do?

879
01:27:03,225 --> 01:27:05,785
Our devotion is only to Nayman!

880
01:27:09,625 --> 01:27:11,735
Here you are, seeing
with your own eyes, Osman.

881
01:27:14,665 --> 01:27:20,835
What I see is the loyalty of the leaders only.

882
01:27:23,055 --> 01:27:27,345
But what about the soldiers below?

883
01:27:29,205 --> 01:27:34,325
A nail can save a horseshoe.
A horseshoe can save a horse.

884
01:27:36,145 --> 01:27:48,685
A horse might save a man, and a man might
lead the entire army to victory or lead it to rebellion

885
01:27:52,405 --> 01:27:58,485
I am still behind my words.
There are rebellion voices in your army.

886
01:28:00,305 --> 01:28:03,345
It's hard to convince you, isn't it?

887
01:28:07,105 --> 01:28:09,145
The same situation exists for you.

888
01:28:09,925 --> 01:28:15,215
It is clear that you will not understand
without seeing and hearing.

889
01:28:16,225 --> 01:28:17,495
Okay then.

890
01:28:23,555 --> 01:28:28,735
Get out there, Nayman, you will answer!

891
01:28:39,635 --> 01:28:45,805
Get out of your tent Nayman!
You have to answer us!

892
01:28:46,275 --> 01:28:50,465
Answer us!
Answer us!

893
01:28:59,905 --> 01:29:02,375
Get out, Nayman, get out!

894
01:29:32,065 --> 01:29:38,655
A commander always listens to his soldiers.

895
01:29:39,085 --> 01:29:41,675
That's the way since The Great Genghis.

896
01:29:42,675 --> 01:29:46,185
Tell me, what is your problem?

897
01:29:50,425 --> 01:29:57,055
Speak or you will die without
me knowing what your problem is!

898
01:29:57,325 --> 01:29:59,375
Why did we come here, Nayman?

899
01:30:01,995 --> 01:30:03,575
Let him talk.

900
01:30:04,025 --> 01:30:05,325
Say.

901
01:30:05,455 --> 01:30:09,535
Ghazan Khan lost his way, and we're behind
you, because you know the way, Nayman

902
01:30:11,685 --> 01:30:13,645
Are you kidding us, Nayman?

903
01:30:13,775 --> 01:30:16,255
Have you united with our enemy, Nayman?

904
01:30:20,415 --> 01:30:23,105
What are you saying?
They say you converted to Islam, Nayman.

905
01:30:27,755 --> 01:30:29,885
The whole army is talking about it

906
01:30:30,755 --> 01:30:34,915
It is true that I united with Muslims.

907
01:30:36,965 --> 01:30:41,125
It is true that I work with a Muslim ruler.

908
01:30:41,425 --> 01:30:46,305
But I am not a Muslim!

909
01:30:54,535 --> 01:30:58,185
Kagan!
Start the rituel!

910
01:32:20,575 --> 01:32:22,825
Sky Tengri!
(Turkish-Mongolian God)

911
01:32:30,825 --> 01:32:37,845
The three soldiers
who spoke will be forgiven.

912
01:32:40,455 --> 01:32:50,505
And the other cowards who did not speak,
those who were scared will be hanged!

913
01:32:51,085 --> 01:32:54,585
As Mighty Commander Nayman commands.

914
01:33:01,595 --> 01:33:07,595
Forgive us, Nayman, forgive us

915
01:33:15,875 --> 01:33:18,205
How did you know about the rebellion?

916
01:33:19,645 --> 01:33:22,805
Do you have spies inside the army?

917
01:33:23,015 --> 01:33:25,535
I am also a part of this army.

918
01:33:26,855 --> 01:33:28,895
I knew this information in advance.

919
01:33:30,975 --> 01:33:34,825
When you came to my tent and met Edebali...

920
01:33:35,485 --> 01:33:40,425
Especially after you recovered my son Orhan,
this rumor was around.

921
01:33:42,675 --> 01:33:45,085
It was clear that this would come up one day.

922
01:33:47,965 --> 01:33:49,665
And I warned you.

923
01:33:50,435 --> 01:33:52,795
Trust is not easily earned.

924
01:33:54,165 --> 01:33:56,305
But it can be easily lost.

925
01:33:59,015 --> 01:34:00,885
Come to the tent.

926
01:34:33,985 --> 01:34:37,325
Now, Hatuns!

927
01:34:37,575 --> 01:34:38,895
Let's go!

928
01:34:38,965 --> 01:34:42,515
Do not leave those who touched childrne alive!

929
01:34:43,835 --> 01:34:46,565
May the hands that extend
to our children be broken!

930
01:35:35,015 --> 01:35:37,845
Children, oh, thank Allah!

931
01:35:37,945 --> 01:35:43,285
Children, thank Allah you survived

932
01:35:43,875 --> 01:35:46,055
Easy, easy, get up.

933
01:35:46,235 --> 01:35:48,625
Come, come, come.

934
01:35:49,295 --> 01:35:50,315
Come here.

935
01:35:51,195 --> 01:35:52,225
Malhun.

936
01:35:55,110 --> 01:35:56,840
Oh thank Allah!

937
01:36:00,975 --> 01:36:03,395
- Are you okay?
- Are you fine?

938
01:36:03,615 --> 01:36:04,925
Alright.

939
01:36:05,525 --> 01:36:07,225
Come and rest now.

940
01:36:07,805 --> 01:36:10,045
You are fine, right?

941
01:36:19,775 --> 01:36:21,365
Malhun.

942
01:36:25,485 --> 01:36:27,535
Come on, thank Allah.

943
01:36:30,165 --> 01:36:31,595
Hey, let's get together.

944
01:36:31,925 --> 01:36:36,475
- Come on, get up, kids
- Mashallah

945
01:36:48,855 --> 01:36:50,865
Tell me, where are the rest of the kids?

946
01:36:51,155 --> 01:36:52,715
I am talking to you!

947
01:36:53,545 --> 01:36:55,625
Talk or I will cut off your head!

948
01:37:02,575 --> 01:37:05,175
We need to find out
where the rest of the children are

949
01:37:05,545 --> 01:37:07,045
Bala Hatun.

950
01:37:07,375 --> 01:37:10,075
Let me find our alps
who pursued them and tell you

951
01:37:10,425 --> 01:37:11,875
Do you know Enulok Cave?

952
01:37:12,675 --> 01:37:14,785
Come over there when you learn.
We'll be there.

953
01:37:18,795 --> 01:37:20,925
What do they want from our children?

954
01:37:21,215 --> 01:37:23,995
They want our children
to rise their swords in our faces.

955
01:37:26,895 --> 01:37:28,155
We cannot allow this.

956
01:37:28,155 --> 01:37:29,455
Of course we will not allow.

957
01:37:30,105 --> 01:37:32,615
Ayse, send word to Aktemur.

958
01:37:32,815 --> 01:37:35,865
They're too many, we're going to need help.

959
01:37:37,045 --> 01:37:38,765
We will send another word.

960
01:37:40,065 --> 01:37:41,395
To whom?

961
01:37:41,435 --> 01:37:43,295
To someone who can help us.

962
01:38:15,725 --> 01:38:17,815
We distributed a portion of the gold, my Bey.

963
01:38:18,515 --> 01:38:20,895
Good, let us lighten our burden.

964
01:38:22,825 --> 01:38:24,175
My Bey.

965
01:38:24,185 --> 01:38:26,905
Will we go to battle when
we're done with the gold?

966
01:38:28,655 --> 01:38:30,985
We will go, Inshallah Kotlu, we will go.

967
01:38:31,615 --> 01:38:35,365
Besides, Hatuns were sorry that Osman Bey
was fighting a hard fight there...

968
01:38:36,065 --> 01:38:39,665
...and the only thing they needed to do
was to share the gold.

969
01:38:41,855 --> 01:38:44,885
Now everyone needs to kill Mongol soldiers!

970
01:38:45,155 --> 01:38:46,545
Let's go.

971
01:39:01,225 --> 01:39:02,735
Come on, come on!

972
01:39:39,985 --> 01:39:41,565
Tell me, what's going on?

973
01:39:41,565 --> 01:39:44,065
They go to distribute
the rest of the gold, my Bey?

974
01:39:44,405 --> 01:39:47,685
Why did they split up with the Hatuns?

975
01:39:47,685 --> 01:39:49,245
Is there news about Osman Bey?

976
01:39:49,245 --> 01:39:52,085
The Hatuns of Kayi tribe
are following the Mongol soldiers.

977
01:39:52,085 --> 01:39:55,565
Also, they said something about Osman Bey.

978
01:39:55,565 --> 01:39:57,085
What are they saying?

979
01:39:57,105 --> 01:40:00,605
Osman Bey is playing
a game on Commander Nayman

980
01:40:03,105 --> 01:40:07,445
You say it at the end
while you need to say it firstly!

981
01:40:10,025 --> 01:40:14,665
Take, you gave me
what is more precious than gold.

982
01:40:15,665 --> 01:40:17,085
We will be back quickly

983
01:40:17,135 --> 01:40:19,215
My Bey, what about the gold?

984
01:40:20,385 --> 01:40:22,945
We have something
more precious than gold, come on!

985
01:40:28,595 --> 01:40:30,685
Nayman's headquarters

986
01:40:38,085 --> 01:40:41,765
Today you did your tasks fully.

987
01:40:42,085 --> 01:40:46,505
I am lucky to have a commander like you.

988
01:40:50,065 --> 01:40:52,845
You put your sword at my command.

989
01:40:53,165 --> 01:40:57,565
And I will give you this sword.

990
01:41:21,205 --> 01:41:22,565
Whose sword is this?

991
01:41:24,905 --> 01:41:32,115
This sword is the sword of a noble Turk
who served Gengish Khan.

992
01:41:32,585 --> 01:41:34,575
It's Noyan's sword.

993
01:41:40,395 --> 01:41:42,165
Noyan huh?

994
01:41:42,365 --> 01:41:47,505
And you will serve me likewise.

995
01:41:59,505 --> 01:42:05,835
And you will reward me like Genghis Khan, huh?

996
01:42:11,965 --> 01:42:14,965
Prepare very well.

997
01:42:14,965 --> 01:42:19,235
I grant you the control of
my army with this sword.

998
01:42:26,965 --> 01:42:29,685
Now that you give me control...

999
01:42:30,505 --> 01:42:34,155
So, I want to know.

1000
01:42:34,915 --> 01:42:38,005
Who is your friend and who is your enemy?

1001
01:42:40,865 --> 01:42:43,555
Aren't you afraid of Ghazan Khan's campaigns?

1002
01:42:46,265 --> 01:42:49,205
I wouldn't be afraid even if I was alone.

1003
01:42:49,885 --> 01:42:52,865
But I am not alone.

1004
01:42:57,315 --> 01:43:00,785
I have a brother, Talay

1005
01:43:01,955 --> 01:43:06,505
He strives with me for the same
end in the lands of the Mamluks

1006
01:43:08,035 --> 01:43:11,945
Gathering the army, gathering supporters.

1007
01:43:12,905 --> 01:43:18,955
He draws both Turk and Mongol Beys
to our side.

1008
01:43:24,845 --> 01:43:31,945
That is, you are the man here
and he is the man there.

1009
01:43:34,425 --> 01:43:37,195
Ghazan Khan is in trouble then.

1010
01:43:37,885 --> 01:43:42,445
Of course, but is he the only one?

1011
01:43:42,805 --> 01:43:48,065
Anyone who dares to stand up to us
is in trouble.

1012
01:43:48,065 --> 01:43:51,925
We'll be the trouble, Osman!

1013
01:43:57,595 --> 01:44:00,755
But there is a deficiency in your campaign.

1014
01:44:03,305 --> 01:44:05,185
I want to say that.

1015
01:44:05,675 --> 01:44:08,865
What is it? Say.

1016
01:44:11,315 --> 01:44:14,915
Everything you say today turns out true.

1017
01:44:19,755 --> 01:44:21,505
You are talking about a state.

1018
01:44:23,715 --> 01:44:28,745
Soldiers are needed for the state,
you have a lot of them.

1019
01:44:31,875 --> 01:44:38,515
When swords are needed...
Your caravans bring you swords

1020
01:44:38,955 --> 01:44:42,205
And if you want gold,
it is also on the way.

1021
01:44:47,765 --> 01:44:49,385
What is the shortage?

1022
01:44:50,635 --> 01:44:56,445
The missing thing is a characteristic
that will give you legitimacy.

1023
01:44:59,245 --> 01:45:01,705
You are not from a noble family.

1024
01:45:03,525 --> 01:45:12,035
No sword, no seal, no banner
left over from Genghis Khan.

1025
01:45:13,685 --> 01:45:19,685
Otherwise, otherwise
why should they stand behind you?

1026
01:45:21,905 --> 01:45:24,825
You are more than I expected.

1027
01:45:27,065 --> 01:45:29,305
I also have them, Osman.

1028
01:45:31,835 --> 01:45:34,595
The hugest.

1029
01:45:38,275 --> 01:45:47,785
There is a seal so big that it shakes the whole world,
not just the Mongols, and makes them line up behind me

1030
01:45:53,505 --> 01:45:56,025
The seal of Gengish Khan.

1031
01:45:59,245 --> 01:46:02,225
That seal is in our hands.

1032
01:46:02,875 --> 01:46:05,425
My brother Talay has it.

1033
01:46:06,555 --> 01:46:11,965
Every letter I write with that seal
will be considered an order.

1034
01:46:12,345 --> 01:46:19,385
All Mongol lords and kings
shall gather under my banner.

1035
01:46:19,885 --> 01:46:24,045
There was only one thing missing
in the state that I will found.

1036
01:46:24,075 --> 01:46:25,985
And it is not the seal.

1037
01:46:29,145 --> 01:46:31,665
And it was skillfull commanders, Osman.

1038
01:46:32,205 --> 01:46:38,405
As long as your sword is with me,
no one will stand against us...

1039
01:46:38,755 --> 01:46:44,035
Everyone, everyone will kneel before us.

1040
01:46:46,945 --> 01:46:48,965
The knee that does not kneel will be broken!

1041
01:46:50,805 --> 01:46:52,965
And the head that does not bow will be cut off!

1042
01:46:52,965 --> 01:46:56,545
My sword is at your command, never worry.

1043
01:46:57,425 --> 01:47:04,105
I'm going to get very big and make you big, Osman.

1044
01:47:06,465 --> 01:47:07,915
Eyvallah.

1045
01:47:10,365 --> 01:47:13,435
So, if you'll excuse me now, I'd like to rest.

1046
01:47:15,715 --> 01:47:21,315
Of course, Commander Osman, of course.

1047
01:47:28,085 --> 01:47:30,145
Oktem's Tents.

1048
01:47:30,840 --> 01:47:32,840
My condolences, Bengi Hatun.

1049
01:47:34,370 --> 01:47:36,950
Your pain is fresh, I know.

1050
01:47:37,780 --> 01:47:42,650
But know that from now on
I will always be by your side.

1051
01:47:43,610 --> 01:47:47,820
When you're in trouble, you'll find me first.

1052
01:47:49,200 --> 01:47:51,620
May Allah bless you, Mother Sultan.

1053
01:47:53,100 --> 01:47:56,070
But I no longer need anyone.

1054
01:47:57,500 --> 01:48:00,010
What do you mean by that, Bengi Hatun?

1055
01:48:01,130 --> 01:48:03,470
Aren't we together like we were?

1056
01:48:04,180 --> 01:48:07,360
Actually we need each other now.

1057
01:48:08,510 --> 01:48:11,010
My husband is gone, Mother Sultan.

1058
01:48:11,650 --> 01:48:14,230
My husband died because of that dog.

1059
01:48:16,380 --> 01:48:18,460
We are all very sad about this.

1060
01:48:19,770 --> 01:48:23,600
Oktem Bey was a valiant Bey.

1061
01:48:25,070 --> 01:48:28,630
We will definitely avenge him.

1062
01:48:30,260 --> 01:48:31,970
Have no doubt about it.

1063
01:48:32,720 --> 01:48:35,560
You will definitely get revenge.

1064
01:48:35,730 --> 01:48:38,720
But we can't undo
what happened to my family.

1065
01:48:39,840 --> 01:48:41,520
The dog, Olof, died.

1066
01:48:41,970 --> 01:48:48,030
And my husband is gone before I rejoice
in the revenge of my brother and my alps.

1067
01:48:48,280 --> 01:48:51,030
I no longer trust anyone.

1068
01:48:53,690 --> 01:48:56,810
Let your pain go away.

1069
01:48:57,540 --> 01:49:00,670
- And then we talk
- This pain does not go away, Mother Sultan.

1070
01:49:02,350 --> 01:49:06,760
If Nayman's head is cut off someday...

1071
01:49:07,730 --> 01:49:09,740
Then maybe my pain will ease.

1072
01:49:10,160 --> 01:49:11,680
But it does not go away.

1073
01:49:14,000 --> 01:49:21,870
This pain will remain with me until
I surrender my soul to the Creator

1074
01:49:22,990 --> 01:49:30,070
I promise we'll decapitate Nayman together

1075
01:49:31,100 --> 01:49:36,180
But first we must increase our strength, Bengi Hatun.

1076
01:49:44,480 --> 01:49:46,840
Who will sit on the throne?

1077
01:49:47,200 --> 01:49:51,690
My son Aktemur will sit on the throne.

1078
01:49:59,720 --> 01:50:02,210
Yenisehir

1079
01:50:11,680 --> 01:50:15,650
So Cerkutay, what are you thinking about?

1080
01:50:16,010 --> 01:50:17,720
Drink your soup and don't let it get cold!

1081
01:50:24,180 --> 01:50:25,450
I'm not hungry.

1082
01:50:25,990 --> 01:50:28,130
If you don't drink it, you can't get up.
Come on.

1083
01:50:28,130 --> 01:50:31,000
I'm not going to drink it,
Ulgen Hatun, I'm not!

1084
01:50:36,730 --> 01:50:38,950
Then don't!

1085
01:50:52,410 --> 01:50:54,990
You broke Ulgen's heart.

1086
01:50:56,780 --> 01:50:59,900
But your heart
hurts the most, doesn't it, Cerkutay?

1087
01:51:03,130 --> 01:51:04,790
Kumral Abdal.

1088
01:51:14,560 --> 01:51:17,120
What are you runnung away from, Cerkutay?

1089
01:51:23,560 --> 01:51:27,180
From the exam, you know, Kumral Abdal.

1090
01:51:27,730 --> 01:51:30,040
You know what's going on.

1091
01:51:34,970 --> 01:51:36,840
I'm afraid.

1092
01:51:38,300 --> 01:51:41,110
I am afraid of taking the exam again.

1093
01:51:45,150 --> 01:51:47,920
You can't run away from your fears, Cerkutay.

1094
01:51:49,090 --> 01:51:52,340
Especially from an exam, y
ou can never run away from it

1095
01:51:52,910 --> 01:51:54,400
What should I do?

1096
01:51:55,130 --> 01:51:58,320
You'll do what you always do, Cerkutay.

1097
01:52:04,760 --> 01:52:07,090
You will listen to your heart.

1098
01:52:09,410 --> 01:52:11,550
Death is certain.

1099
01:52:12,530 --> 01:52:15,010
You live what Allah has written for you.

1100
01:52:17,010 --> 01:52:19,670
You can't escape life either, Cerkutay.

1101
01:52:22,420 --> 01:52:24,820
You'll heal the broken hearts.

1102
01:52:25,830 --> 01:52:27,700
Life is short.

1103
01:52:27,880 --> 01:52:32,020
Life is too short to break a heart.

1104
01:52:44,950 --> 01:52:46,270
Eyvallah
(thank you)

1105
01:52:48,510 --> 01:52:50,170
So they are in Tasdelen.

1106
01:52:52,850 --> 01:52:54,630
That place is not suitable for battle.

1107
01:52:56,350 --> 01:52:57,910
How many are they?

1108
01:52:58,030 --> 01:52:59,350
I counted 50 people.

1109
01:52:59,350 --> 01:53:01,350
There are around 10 children.

1110
01:53:04,670 --> 01:53:07,760
When they find out that the soldiers
we slaughtered don't come...

1111
01:53:07,760 --> 01:53:10,160
...they will understand that
there is a problem.

1112
01:53:10,160 --> 01:53:14,110
For that reason,
we will attack them at the crack of dawn.

1113
01:53:15,330 --> 01:53:16,870
Malhun.

1114
01:53:16,970 --> 01:53:19,110
We have sent alps to the mansion.

1115
01:53:19,110 --> 01:53:21,110
We are just 15 people.

1116
01:53:21,970 --> 01:53:24,530
Will we be able to beat them in your opinion?

1117
01:53:24,810 --> 01:53:26,330
Of course.

1118
01:53:27,230 --> 01:53:29,530
Osman Bey risks his life in front of his enemies

1119
01:53:30,110 --> 01:53:32,270
I hope we will succeed in this.

1120
01:53:34,590 --> 01:53:38,230
Aktemur, any news from Osman Bey?

1121
01:53:51,230 --> 01:53:52,950
Is there anything else you want, Osman Bey?

1122
01:53:53,530 --> 01:53:55,990
No, thank you.

1123
01:54:03,950 --> 01:54:05,410
The seal of Gengish Khan.

1124
01:54:07,030 --> 01:54:09,850
That seal is in our hands.

1125
01:54:10,690 --> 01:54:13,050
Take it to my brother Talay.

1126
01:54:14,330 --> 01:54:19,090
Every letter I write with
that seal will count as an order

1127
01:54:20,090 --> 01:54:27,110
And all the Mongol leaders
and their kingdoms will gather under my banner

1128
01:54:40,370 --> 01:54:42,870
You will drown in your dreams.

1129
01:54:44,210 --> 01:54:46,230
Without that seal...

1130
01:54:47,470 --> 01:54:51,010
The country you will create
will become your tomb.

1131
01:54:51,950 --> 01:54:53,730
It will become your grave.

1132
01:54:58,110 --> 01:55:00,690
And the state I'll found will rise.

1133
01:55:03,685 --> 01:55:06,714
Nayman's Headquarters.

1134
01:55:22,170 --> 01:55:23,670
Osman is here.

1135
01:55:26,890 --> 01:55:29,010
He will pay for his actions.

1136
01:55:30,670 --> 01:55:33,690
Stop, let's see why he is here first.

1137
01:55:34,930 --> 01:55:37,450
Why do you look like a deadhead?

1138
01:55:37,450 --> 01:55:38,950
Come on.

1139
01:55:45,690 --> 01:55:47,050
Come on.

1140
01:55:48,110 --> 01:55:49,830
Come to me.

1141
01:55:52,050 --> 01:55:53,590
Come on.

1142
01:56:02,050 --> 01:56:03,390
Get away!

1143
01:56:14,940 --> 01:56:16,700
Commander Neyman!

1144
01:56:18,440 --> 01:56:20,140
Commander Neyman!

1145
01:56:28,760 --> 01:56:31,280
Commander Neyman, I have news!

1146
01:56:51,960 --> 01:56:54,040
Where is my gold?

1147
01:56:54,340 --> 01:56:56,340
I don't see it.

1148
01:56:58,080 --> 01:57:02,800
I have brought you something
more valuable than gold, Commander Nayman

1149
01:57:06,520 --> 01:57:07,820
What is it?

1150
01:57:12,200 --> 01:57:14,280
Osman Bey.

1151
01:57:18,040 --> 01:57:20,080
What's wrong with him?

1152
01:57:24,700 --> 01:57:27,240
He's cheating again.

1153
01:57:30,600 --> 01:57:33,380
He allied with you to get information.

1154
01:57:35,960 --> 01:57:38,500
He still wants you dead.

1155
01:57:40,720 --> 01:57:42,460
Osman.

1156
01:57:44,640 --> 01:57:47,860
You're curious as to
why I'm here, aren't you?

1157
01:57:57,820 --> 01:58:00,180
In order to put out the fire that is about to rage

1158
01:58:06,920 --> 01:58:09,660
Catch Osman!

1159
01:58:09,740 --> 01:58:11,300
Come on hurry up!

1160
01:58:12,240 --> 01:58:15,740
Osman, catch Osman. Find Osman.

1161
01:58:15,740 --> 01:58:19,700
Catch Osman!
Catch Osman!

1162
01:58:19,700 --> 01:58:22,180
- Come on
- Don't let him run away.

1163
01:58:22,740 --> 01:58:26,460
Catch Osman!

1164
01:58:26,460 --> 01:58:27,980
Osman escaped!

1165
01:58:28,770 --> 01:58:30,330
He escaped!

1166
01:59:01,290 --> 01:59:02,880
Where is Osman?

1167
01:59:24,820 --> 01:59:26,330
Osman!

1168
01:59:30,630 --> 01:59:32,470
Bring Osman to me!

1169
01:59:33,000 --> 01:59:34,780
Now you're done, Osman!

1170
01:59:38,680 --> 01:59:41,250
Osman is escaping!
Osman is escaping!

1171
01:59:41,610 --> 01:59:43,140
Osman is escaping!

1172
02:00:05,360 --> 02:00:08,440
He will take the seal!
He will take the seal!

1173
02:00:10,440 --> 02:00:14,500
He heard about my plans and Talay!

1174
02:00:15,320 --> 02:00:18,170
Talay builds an army there!

1175
02:00:18,490 --> 02:00:20,410
The seal must be mine!

1176
02:00:20,630 --> 02:00:23,930
I was going to command the Beys
with that seal!

1177
02:00:24,660 --> 02:00:26,780
Our armies were going to unite!

1178
02:00:27,060 --> 02:00:29,780
We were going to destroy our enemies!

1179
02:00:29,980 --> 02:00:31,930
Osman knows this!

1180
02:00:32,170 --> 02:00:34,060
He'll try to be me.

1181
02:00:34,310 --> 02:00:36,360
Goktalha, kill him!

1182
02:00:36,460 --> 02:00:38,970
Osman will never reach his goal.

1183
02:00:40,970 --> 02:00:43,110
Commander, what about you?

1184
02:00:45,500 --> 02:00:47,900
I promised them.

1185
02:00:48,820 --> 02:00:51,190
Now I will keep my promise.

1186
02:01:17,885 --> 02:01:22,475
Nayman's arrival changed the whole game.

1187
02:01:24,385 --> 02:01:29,915
No matter what happens, the palace
must stand still.

1188
02:01:31,555 --> 02:01:35,085
I strive only for this, Mother Sultan.

1189
02:01:39,575 --> 02:01:43,395
If Nayman hurts even
one person in this land...

1190
02:01:44,785 --> 02:01:51,105
And if you do not prevent the Sultan
from being harmed while you are the Vizier....

1191
02:01:52,535 --> 02:01:55,035
Then consider yourself dead, Saveli.

1192
02:01:57,935 --> 02:02:02,815
Both my life and death is for
the supreme Seljuk state, Mother Sultan.

1193
02:02:03,665 --> 02:02:07,395
We will find all the connections
Mongols have, and erase them.

1194
02:02:13,235 --> 02:02:17,375
Who is Nayman's spy in Konya?

1195
02:02:17,775 --> 02:02:19,155
And where is he?

1196
02:02:19,975 --> 02:02:22,135
First we will find him.

1197
02:02:23,575 --> 02:02:25,635
We are after him, Mother Sultan.

1198
02:02:27,025 --> 02:02:31,075
When I find him, I will kill him myself.

1199
02:02:37,095 --> 02:02:39,765
We are going beyond the Seljuk state.

1200
02:02:43,895 --> 02:02:46,215
Nayman will raise the banner of rebellion.

1201
02:02:47,335 --> 02:02:49,455
They will take over the throne of Ghazan Khan.

1202
02:02:50,095 --> 02:02:53,875
The peace started by Ilkhanate will end.

1203
02:02:54,465 --> 02:02:56,485
Their intention is to shed blood.

1204
02:02:59,335 --> 02:03:01,715
What is there beyond the Seljuq state, my Bey?

1205
02:03:02,515 --> 02:03:05,795
Talay, Nayman's brother, has the seal.

1206
02:03:06,945 --> 02:03:10,325
He established his army with
the strength he took from the Beys of Mamluk.

1207
02:03:12,725 --> 02:03:14,195
Nayman did the same thing.

1208
02:03:15,105 --> 02:03:19,455
Since his arrival,
he has got along with the Beys.

1209
02:03:19,905 --> 02:03:23,735
He wanted to make me his commander
and he wanted gold too.

1210
02:03:24,615 --> 02:03:26,695
Their intention is not this land.

1211
02:03:26,895 --> 02:03:29,525
- What is their aim then, my Bey?
- Tabriz!

1212
02:03:33,415 --> 02:03:35,555
They want to take over the throne of Ghazan Khan!

1213
02:03:36,675 --> 02:03:40,485
And they want to rule that land.

1214
02:03:43,375 --> 02:03:45,575
And when they get what they want..

1215
02:03:46,215 --> 02:03:49,425
We are the ones whose blood
will be shed the most, right, my Bey?

1216
02:03:50,465 --> 02:03:53,775
They need the seal to break us.

1217
02:03:54,495 --> 02:03:56,565
The seal is in Talay's hands now.

1218
02:03:57,935 --> 02:04:00,485
It's a seal from Genghis Khan's council.

1219
02:04:00,785 --> 02:04:04,245
If you have the seal,
everything you say becomes an order.

1220
02:04:04,375 --> 02:04:07,955
That's why we won't let Nayman take it.

1221
02:04:09,235 --> 02:04:10,455
We'll take it.

1222
02:04:12,645 --> 02:04:15,205
That's our only shot.

1223
02:04:15,695 --> 02:04:20,355
If we fail, they'll found a state whose
only aim is to erase Islam from these lands.

1224
02:04:24,465 --> 02:04:26,755
Since we are the swords of Islam...

1225
02:04:27,535 --> 02:04:30,495
Let's pierce the heart of enemies!

1226
02:04:30,805 --> 02:04:32,955
We will never allow them!

1227
02:04:33,135 --> 02:04:34,675
Eyvallah (Yes) my Bey!

1228
02:04:34,675 --> 02:04:35,975
Let's go!

1229
02:05:31,015 --> 02:05:35,365
- Come on, sisters!
- Come on Alps! Kill the ignoble!

1230
02:05:35,365 --> 02:05:39,495
- Allah is eternal!
- Allah is righteous!

1231
02:06:50,835 --> 02:06:52,545
Watch your backs!

1232
02:06:55,895 --> 02:06:59,635
Sisters, we won't stop until
we kill 5 of them, let's go!

1233
02:07:03,535 --> 02:07:06,775
Brother, why don't we practice?

1234
02:07:12,115 --> 02:07:13,615
Is it...

1235
02:07:17,880 --> 02:07:20,460
If I take my sword out of its scabbard,
you will fall to the ground, my brother.

1236
02:07:20,460 --> 02:07:23,910
Let it out then, brother,
I am not afraid of you.

1237
02:07:29,750 --> 02:07:33,130
Come on brother, you must be rusty.

1238
02:07:35,560 --> 02:07:38,620
You are out of your mind.
I will knock you down now.

1239
02:07:38,970 --> 02:07:41,130
- Allah is eternal.
- Allah is righteous.

1240
02:08:22,585 --> 02:08:24,154
Come on brother.

1241
02:08:45,960 --> 02:08:47,810
No, brother.

1242
02:08:50,040 --> 02:08:51,630
My hand does not obey me.

1243
02:08:56,810 --> 02:09:00,220
- You'll get better, brother, Also Kumral Ab...
- No!

1244
02:09:01,080 --> 02:09:02,220
No Aladdin.

1245
02:09:04,860 --> 02:09:07,180
Don't tell anyone that my hand is not working.

1246
02:09:14,650 --> 02:09:17,190
I will not bring pain into my family's heart
at this difficult time.

1247
02:09:19,260 --> 02:09:21,050
I won't tell them brother.

1248
02:09:21,180 --> 02:09:25,180
But you will not surrender
and you will not be defeated, my brother!

1249
02:10:36,010 --> 02:10:38,010
No backup on the way, Bala?

1250
02:10:40,610 --> 02:10:41,990
Hold on a little longer!

1251
02:10:42,090 --> 02:10:43,440
I am here, Hatuns!

1252
02:11:38,660 --> 02:11:40,410
You shameless soldiers!

1253
02:11:41,090 --> 02:11:43,090
I will burn anyone who touches children!

1254
02:11:51,890 --> 02:11:54,930
We won't stop until
we chop everyone's throats off!

1255
02:11:55,180 --> 02:11:56,530
Come on!

1256
02:12:10,300 --> 02:12:12,110
Obviously we are not alone!

1257
02:12:13,110 --> 02:12:14,850
Come on!

1258
02:12:40,970 --> 02:12:42,300
Children!

1259
02:12:44,490 --> 02:12:45,860
Children!

1260
02:12:49,810 --> 02:12:52,130
It's over, my children, it's over.

1261
02:12:52,300 --> 02:12:54,800
Come to me, Come!

1262
02:12:55,150 --> 02:12:57,650
Thank Allah that all of you survived

1263
02:12:59,380 --> 02:13:01,480
Come on, come on, come on, come on

1264
02:13:03,450 --> 02:13:06,160
Praise be to Allah, go down slowly,
go down slowly, go down slowly

1265
02:13:13,500 --> 02:13:14,510
Let's go

1266
02:13:14,800 --> 02:13:15,920
Thank Allah.

1267
02:13:16,100 --> 02:13:19,160
Thank Allah, children, thank Allah.

1268
02:13:19,340 --> 02:13:20,380
Come on baby, come on.

1269
02:13:20,560 --> 02:13:21,590
Bring water!

1270
02:13:21,810 --> 02:13:24,590
You will all get back to your mothers.

1271
02:13:29,910 --> 02:13:32,910
You caught us just in time, Bengi Hatun.

1272
02:13:33,100 --> 02:13:35,840
You told us at the right time.

1273
02:13:36,160 --> 02:13:38,050
When I got the news, I felt so proud.

1274
02:13:38,240 --> 02:13:39,550
Since we are relatives now...

1275
02:13:39,700 --> 02:13:41,590
...we'll have each other's backs,
won't we, Bengi Hatun?

1276
02:13:44,910 --> 02:13:46,780
Come on, come on baby, come on.

1277
02:14:13,390 --> 02:14:14,940
Osman's son.

1278
02:14:27,720 --> 02:14:29,740
Tengri(God) healed you

1279
02:14:30,890 --> 02:14:33,100
But you lost your way.

1280
02:15:00,270 --> 02:15:01,850
Osman is coming.

1281
02:15:03,010 --> 02:15:05,030
The arrow has come out of the bow.

1282
02:15:06,440 --> 02:15:08,290
I want Osman.

1283
02:15:08,760 --> 02:15:10,220
Are you well prepared?

1284
02:15:10,330 --> 02:15:11,900
Yes sir.

1285
02:15:15,340 --> 02:15:16,690
Let's go.

1286
02:15:43,525 --> 02:15:45,585
Alps, it's a trap!

1287
02:15:56,935 --> 02:15:59,005
Sir, they're surrounding us.

1288
02:16:08,495 --> 02:16:10,635
Erlik Khan is our guide.

1289
02:16:11,315 --> 02:16:13,015
And war is our wedding!

1290
02:16:14,745 --> 02:16:16,835
Your head is our share, Osman!

1291
02:16:18,455 --> 02:16:21,225
Sir, these dogs are surrounding all over us.

1292
02:16:21,575 --> 02:16:23,645
We'll send horses at them
and surprise them!

1293
02:16:24,495 --> 02:16:26,065
And then we'll form the shield system!

1294
02:16:26,115 --> 02:16:27,445
Come on, be prepared!

1295
02:16:27,505 --> 02:16:28,555
Okay my Bey!

1296
02:16:33,264 --> 02:16:34,844
Come on! Now!

1297
02:16:43,714 --> 02:16:45,294
Take cover!

1298
02:17:47,325 --> 02:17:49,905
Sir, we are out of arrow.

1299
02:18:00,584 --> 02:18:02,384
Come to us, come to us.

1300
02:18:20,850 --> 02:18:30,459
Visit our website for more: turkision.com